window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 24 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000071181","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"MONEY\" is written as \"PRQHB.\" How will \"THINK\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"MONEY\" को \"PRQHB\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"THINK\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"WLKQN"},"2":{"en":"WLKQN"},"3":{"en":"WNPMT"},"4":{"en":"WMNKT"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In MONEY each letter is replaced by the letter three places ahead of it: M&#8594;P, O&#8594;R, N&#8594;Q, E&#8594;H and Y&#8594;B (wrapping past Z), which gives PRQHB<br>Applying the same +3 step to THINK: T&#8594;W, H&#8594;K, I&#8594;L, N&#8594;Q and K&#8594;N, so the code is W K L Q N<br>The printed options show WLKQN, that is with the second and third letters interchanged, so the exact code is not printed in any option and the options carry this error<br>SSC has given this answer in the official answer key, so the key value WLKQN is kept<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): WLKQN.</b>","hi":"MONEY में प्रत्येक अक्षर को तीन स्थान आगे का अक्षर बनाया जाता है: M&#8594;P, O&#8594;R, N&#8594;Q, E&#8594;H तथा Y&#8594;B (Z के आगे घूमकर), जिससे PRQHB मिलता है<br>THINK पर वही +3 चरण लगाने से T&#8594;W, H&#8594;K, I&#8594;L, N&#8594;Q तथा K&#8594;N, अतः कूट W K L Q N है<br>मुद्रित विकल्पों में WLKQN है, अर्थात् दूसरा और तीसरा अक्षर परस्पर बदले हुए हैं, इसलिए सटीक कूट किसी विकल्प में मुद्रित नहीं है और विकल्पों में यही त्रुटि है<br>SSC ने आधिकारिक उत्तर कुंजी में यही उत्तर दिया है, अतः कुंजी का मान WLKQN ही रखा गया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): WLKQN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000071182","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, if '457' means 'POLITY IS SCIENCE', '712' means 'SCIENCE MUST TRUE', and '189' means 'TRUE PERSON LESS', then which numeral stands for 'SCIENCE'? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में यदि '457' का अर्थ 'POLITY IS SCIENCE' है, '712' का अर्थ 'SCIENCE MUST TRUE' है तथा '189' का अर्थ 'TRUE PERSON LESS' है, तो कौन-सा अंक 'SCIENCE' के लिए है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"SCIENCE appears in 457 and in 712, and the digit common to both codes is 7<br>So 7 stands for SCIENCE, while 4 and 5 belong to POLITY and IS and 1 and 2 belong to MUST and TRUE<br>Hence 7 is the numeral for SCIENCE<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 7.</b>","hi":"SCIENCE, 457 तथा 712 दोनों में आता है, और दोनों कूटों में साझा अंक 7 है<br>अतः 7 का अर्थ SCIENCE है, जबकि 4 और 5 का संबंध POLITY तथा IS से और 1 और 2 का संबंध MUST तथा TRUE से है<br>इसलिए SCIENCE के लिए अंक 7 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000071183","section":"REASONING","topic":"Age Problems","question":{"en":"The present ages of A and B are in the ratio 11 : 14. Eight years ago, their ages were in the ratio 7 : 10. What will be B's age after 6 years? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A और B की वर्तमान आयु का अनुपात 11 : 14 है। आठ वर्ष पहले उनकी आयु का अनुपात 7 : 10 था। 6 वर्ष बाद B की आयु क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42 years","hi":"42 वर्ष"},"2":{"en":"34 years","hi":"34 वर्ष"},"3":{"en":"44 years","hi":"44 वर्ष"},"4":{"en":"38 years","hi":"38 वर्ष"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the present ages be 11x and 14x<br>Eight years ago: (11x − 8) : (14x − 8) = 7 : 10, so 10(11x − 8) = 7(14x − 8), that is 110x − 80 = 98x − 56 and 12x = 24, giving x = 2<br>So B's present age is 14 × 2 = 28 years and after 6 years it will be 34 years<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 34 years.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए वर्तमान आयु 11x तथा 14x है<br>आठ वर्ष पहले: (11x − 8) : (14x − 8) = 7 : 10, अतः 10(11x − 8) = 7(14x − 8), अर्थात् 110x − 80 = 98x − 56 तथा 12x = 24, जिससे x = 2<br>अतः B की वर्तमान आयु 14 × 2 = 28 वर्ष है और 6 वर्ष बाद 34 वर्ष होगी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 34 वर्ष है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000071184","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A vessel contains milk and water in the ratio 13 : 5. If 24 litres of water are added, the ratio becomes 13 : 9. What was the initial quantity of milk? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बर्तन में दूध और पानी का अनुपात 13 : 5 है। यदि 24 लीटर पानी मिलाया जाए तो अनुपात 13 : 9 हो जाता है। दूध की प्रारंभिक मात्रा क्या थी? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"52 litres","hi":"52 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"65 litres","hi":"65 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"78 litres","hi":"78 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"91 litres","hi":"91 लीटर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the milk and water be 13x and 5x, and milk stays the same at 13x while the water becomes 5x + 24<br>Now 13x : (5x + 24) = 13 : 9, so 9x = 5x + 24 and 4x = 24, giving x = 6<br>So the initial quantity of milk is 13 × 6 = 78 litres<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 78 litres.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए दूध और पानी 13x तथा 5x हैं, और दूध 13x ही रहता है जबकि पानी 5x + 24 हो जाता है<br>अब 13x : (5x + 24) = 13 : 9, अतः 9x = 5x + 24 तथा 4x = 24, जिससे x = 6<br>अतः दूध की प्रारंभिक मात्रा 13 × 6 = 78 लीटर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 78 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000071185","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Four options are given below, out of which three are similar in a certain way while one is different. Identify the option that is different from the others. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी निश्चित प्रकार से समान हैं जबकि एक भिन्न है। वह विकल्प पहचानिए जो अन्य से भिन्न है। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dog : Animal"},"2":{"en":"Rose : Flower"},"3":{"en":"Apple : Fruit"},"4":{"en":"Vehicle : Bus"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first three pairs the first word is one particular member of the class named by the second word: a dog is an animal, a rose is a flower and an apple is a fruit<br>In the fourth pair the order is reversed, because a bus is a type of vehicle and not the other way round<br>So Vehicle : Bus is different from the others<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Vehicle : Bus.</b>","hi":"पहले तीन युग्मों में पहला शब्द दूसरे शब्द से बताई गई श्रेणी का एक विशेष सदस्य है: कुत्ता एक पशु है, गुलाब एक फूल है तथा सेब एक फल है<br>चौथे युग्म में क्रम उलटा है, क्योंकि बस वाहन का एक प्रकार है, इसका विपरीत नहीं<br>अतः Vehicle : Bus अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Vehicle : Bus है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000071186","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Four options are given below, out of which three are similar in a certain way while one is different. Identify the option that is different from the others. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"नीचे चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी निश्चित प्रकार से समान हैं जबकि एक भिन्न है। वह विकल्प पहचानिए जो अन्य से भिन्न है। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Square, Rectangle, Parallelogram"},"2":{"en":"Triangle, Pentagon, Hexagon"},"3":{"en":"Circle, Triangle, Oval"},"4":{"en":"Cube, Cone, Sphere"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first three options all the shapes are plane (two-dimensional) figures<br>In the fourth option the cube, the cone and the sphere are all three-dimensional solids<br>So the fourth option is different from the others<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Cube, Cone, Sphere.</b>","hi":"पहले तीन विकल्पों में सभी आकृतियाँ समतल (द्वि-आयामी) हैं<br>चौथे विकल्प में घन, शंकु तथा गोला सभी त्रि-आयामी ठोस हैं<br>अतः चौथा विकल्प अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Cube, Cone, Sphere है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000071187","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following number series?<br>4, 10, 24, 17, 168, 26, 1344, 37, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित संख्या श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>4, 10, 24, 17, 168, 26, 1344, 37, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12096"},"2":{"en":"32480"},"3":{"en":"46820"},"4":{"en":"12890"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The series interleaves two patterns. The small terms are 4, 10, 17, 26 and 37, which follow n² + 1 for n = 3, 4, 5 and 6 in 10, 17, 26 and 37 ✔<br>The big terms start with 24 and then multiply by 7 and 8: 24 × 7 = 168 ✔ and 168 × 8 = 1344 ✔<br>So the next big term is 1344 × 9 = 12096<br>Hence the missing number is 12096<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 12096.</b>","hi":"श्रेणी में दो पैटर्न एक-दूसरे के बीच चलते हैं। छोटे पद 4, 10, 17, 26 तथा 37 हैं, जिनमें 10, 17, 26 तथा 37 के लिए n² + 1 लागू होता है (n = 3, 4, 5, 6) ✔<br>बड़े पद 24 से शुरू होकर 7 तथा 8 से गुणा होते हैं: 24 × 7 = 168 ✔ तथा 168 × 8 = 1344 ✔<br>अतः अगला बड़ा पद 1344 × 9 = 12096 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 12096 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 12096 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000071188","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What should come in place of question mark (?) in the following number series?<br>6, 12, 48, 19, 480, 28, 5760, 39, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित संख्या श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>6, 12, 48, 19, 480, 28, 5760, 39, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34685"},"2":{"en":"80640"},"3":{"en":"32668"},"4":{"en":"80448"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The series interleaves two patterns. The small terms are 6, 12, 19, 28 and 39, and from the second term onward they follow n² + 3 for n = 3, 4, 5 and 6: 9 + 3 = 12 ✔, 16 + 3 = 19 ✔, 25 + 3 = 28 ✔ and 36 + 3 = 39 ✔<br>The big terms are 48, 480 and 5760, so each is multiplied by 10 and then 12: 48 × 10 = 480 ✔ and 480 × 12 = 5760 ✔<br>So the next big term is 5760 × 14 = 80640<br>Hence the missing number is 80640<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 80640.</b>","hi":"श्रेणी में दो पैटर्न एक-दूसरे के बीच चलते हैं। छोटे पद 6, 12, 19, 28 तथा 39 हैं और दूसरे पद से n² + 3 बनता है (n = 3, 4, 5, 6): 9 + 3 = 12 ✔, 16 + 3 = 19 ✔, 25 + 3 = 28 ✔ तथा 36 + 3 = 39 ✔<br>बड़े पद 48, 480 तथा 5760 हैं, जिनमें प्रत्येक 10 और फिर 12 से गुणा होता है: 48 × 10 = 480 ✔ तथा 480 × 12 = 5760 ✔<br>अतः अगला बड़ा पद 5760 × 14 = 80640 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 80640 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 80640 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000071189","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"There are 48 players in a row. If Karan is 18th from the top, what is his rank from the bottom? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक पंक्ति में 48 खिलाड़ी हैं। यदि करण ऊपर से 18वें स्थान पर है, तो नीचे से उसका स्थान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"29th","hi":"29वाँ"},"2":{"en":"30th","hi":"30वाँ"},"3":{"en":"31st","hi":"31वाँ"},"4":{"en":"32nd","hi":"32वाँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rank from the bottom = total number − rank from the top + 1<br>= 48 − 18 + 1 = 31<br>So Karan's rank from the bottom is 31st<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 31st.</b>","hi":"नीचे से स्थान = कुल संख्या − ऊपर से स्थान + 1<br>= 48 − 18 + 1 = 31<br>अतः नीचे से करण का स्थान 31वाँ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 31वाँ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000071190","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The argument 'No effective vaccine has zero side effects; this drug has zero side effects; therefore, this drug is not an effective vaccine' is [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"तर्क 'किसी भी प्रभावी टीके के शून्य दुष्प्रभाव नहीं होते; इस दवा के दुष्प्रभाव शून्य हैं; इसलिए यह दवा प्रभावी टीका नहीं है' है [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Valid and sound","hi":"वैध तथा यथार्थ"},"2":{"en":"Valid and unsound","hi":"वैध तथा अयथार्थ"},"3":{"en":"Invalid and sound","hi":"अवैध तथा यथार्थ"},"4":{"en":"Invalid and unsound","hi":"अवैध तथा अयथार्थ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The reasoning has the form: no effective vaccine has zero side effects, and this drug has zero side effects, so it is not an effective vaccine<br>This is a correct use of the rule (if a thing has zero side effects it falls outside the class of effective vaccines), so the argument is valid<br>The first premise, however, is factually false, because effective vaccines do have side effects, so the argument is not sound<br>Hence the argument is valid and unsound<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Valid and unsound.</b>","hi":"तर्क का रूप है: किसी प्रभावी टीके के शून्य दुष्प्रभाव नहीं होते, इस दवा के दुष्प्रभाव शून्य हैं, अतः यह प्रभावी टीका नहीं है<br>यह नियम का सही प्रयोग है, अतः तर्क वैध है<br>परंतु पहला आधार वस्तुतः असत्य है, क्योंकि प्रभावी टीकों के दुष्प्रभाव होते हैं, अतः तर्क यथार्थ नहीं है<br>इसलिए तर्क वैध तथा अयथार्थ है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): वैध तथा अयथार्थ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000071191","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90c8-6a99-7c83-a8fc-ef46d6ef09c1_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964761997\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न पूरा करने के लिए चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनिए:<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019e90c8-6a99-7c83-a8fc-ef46d6ef09c1_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090515396\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1192ae5f49b5_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964791535\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a791c2c2432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090538553\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1193baf64387_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964822549\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a79269388294_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090562293\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-11942a66a5f6_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964857027\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a793b69ea92f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090586895\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1195e2026901_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964883839\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a794c5e98ca5_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090610112\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is built symmetrically about its vertical central line: a black banded shape at the top and a large black triangle below, with a small dark dot lying exactly on the central line<br>The missing left half must therefore repeat the same slanting white bands inside a black triangle, and the dark dot on the axis belongs to both halves, so a full circle cannot appear in the answer<br>Option D shows a full circle, option B shows crossing lines that are not in the original and option C carries an extra vertical line, so only the figure of option 1 completes the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1192ae5f49b5_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964791535\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) अपनी ऊर्ध्व मध्य रेखा के सापेक्ष सममित है: ऊपर काली पट्टीदार आकृति और नीचे बड़ा काला त्रिभुज है, तथा छोटा काला बिंदु ठीक मध्य रेखा पर है<br>अतः लुप्त बायाँ आधा काले त्रिभुज के भीतर वही तिरछी सफ़ेद पट्टियाँ दोहराता है, और मध्य रेखा पर पड़ा बिंदु दोनों हिस्सों का साझा है, इसलिए उत्तर में पूरा वृत्त नहीं आ सकता<br>विकल्प D में पूरा वृत्त है, विकल्प B में मूल में न होने वाली काटती रेखाएँ हैं तथा विकल्प C में अतिरिक्त ऊर्ध्व रेखा है, अतः केवल विकल्प 1 की आकृति पैटर्न पूरा करती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a791c2c2432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090538553\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90c8-6a99-7c83-a8fc-ef46d6ef09c1_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964761997","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019e90c8-6a99-7c83-a8fc-ef46d6ef09c1_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090515396"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1192ae5f49b5_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964791535","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a791c2c2432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090538553"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1193baf64387_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964822549","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a79269388294_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090562293"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-11942a66a5f6_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964857027","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a793b69ea92f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090586895"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1195e2026901_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964883839","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a794c5e98ca5_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090610112"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019e90ce-5d8e-7d6f-b214-1192ae5f49b5_EN.jpg?edu=639294380964791535","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ebaab-a7ee-773b-835d-a791c2c2432f_HI.jpg?edu=639294381090538553"]}},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000071192","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If P stands for '÷', Q stands for '×', R stands for '+', and S stands for '−', then what is the value of the following expression?<br>40 P 8 Q 5 R (12 S 6 Q 2) P 3 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि P का अर्थ '÷', Q का अर्थ '×', R का अर्थ '+' तथा S का अर्थ '−' है, तो निम्नलिखित व्यंजक का मान क्या है?<br>40 P 8 Q 5 R (12 S 6 Q 2) P 3 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"32"},"2":{"en":"28"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"35"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Replacing the letters, the expression becomes 40 ÷ 8 × 5 + (12 − 6 × 2) ÷ 3<br>12 − 6 × 2 = 12 − 12 = 0, so the bracket is 0<br>40 ÷ 8 = 5, then 5 × 5 = 25, and 0 ÷ 3 = 0, so the value is 25 + 0 = 25<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 25.</b>","hi":"अक्षरों को बदलने पर व्यंजक 40 ÷ 8 × 5 + (12 − 6 × 2) ÷ 3 बनता है<br>12 − 6 × 2 = 12 − 12 = 0, अतः कोष्ठक का मान 0 है<br>40 ÷ 8 = 5, फिर 5 × 5 = 25 तथा 0 ÷ 3 = 0, अतः मान 25 + 0 = 25 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000071193","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 4 @ 3 @ 2 = 29 and 5 @ 1 @ 4 = 42, what is the value of A in A @ 2 @ 3 = 38? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि 4 @ 3 @ 2 = 29 तथा 5 @ 1 @ 4 = 42 है, तो A @ 2 @ 3 = 38 में A का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The pattern is first² + second² + third²: 16 + 9 + 4 = 29 ✔ and 25 + 1 + 16 = 42 ✔<br>So A² + 4 + 9 = 38, which gives A² = 25 and A = 5<br>Hence the value of A is 5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न है पहला² + दूसरा² + तीसरा²: 16 + 9 + 4 = 29 ✔ तथा 25 + 1 + 16 = 42 ✔<br>अतः A² + 4 + 9 = 38, जिससे A² = 25 तथा A = 5<br>इसलिए A का मान 5 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000071194","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Air pollution is increasing in major cities due to rising vehicle emissions. Excessive smoke leads to respiratory diseases among urban populations.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Vehicle emissions are a major cause of air pollution.<br>II. All respiratory diseases are caused only by air pollution. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>बढ़ते वाहन उत्सर्जन के कारण बड़े शहरों में वायु प्रदूषण बढ़ रहा है। अत्यधिक धुआँ शहरी आबादी में श्वसन रोगों को जन्म देता है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. वाहन उत्सर्जन वायु प्रदूषण का एक प्रमुख कारण है।<br>II. सभी श्वसन रोग केवल वायु प्रदूषण से होते हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither Conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement directly says that air pollution is increasing because of rising vehicle emissions, so vehicle emissions are a major cause of air pollution and I follows<br>It only says that excessive smoke causes respiratory diseases; it never says that all respiratory diseases have this single cause, so II does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"कथन सीधे कहता है कि बढ़ते वाहन उत्सर्जन के कारण वायु प्रदूषण बढ़ रहा है, अतः वाहन उत्सर्जन वायु प्रदूषण का एक प्रमुख कारण है और I निकलता है<br>कथन केवल यह कहता है कि अत्यधिक धुआँ श्वसन रोगों को जन्म देता है; यह नहीं कहता कि सभी श्वसन रोगों का यही एकमात्र कारण है, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000071195","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Despite the government providing heavy subsidies on electric vehicles (EVs), the sales of internal combustion engine (ICE) petrol and diesel cars grew by 12% this fiscal year.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Government subsidies alone are not sufficient to make consumers completely switch to electric vehicles.<br>II. Petrol and diesel cars are cheaper to maintain than electric vehicles. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। निष्कर्षों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-सा कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सरकार द्वारा इलेक्ट्रिक वाहनों (EV) पर भारी सब्सिडी दिए जाने के बावजूद, इस वित्त वर्ष में आंतरिक दहन इंजन (ICE) पेट्रोल तथा डीज़ल कारों की बिक्री 12% बढ़ी।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. केवल सरकारी सब्सिडी उपभोक्ताओं को पूर्णतः इलेक्ट्रिक वाहनों की ओर मोड़ने के लिए पर्याप्त नहीं है।<br>II. पेट्रोल तथा डीज़ल कारों का रखरखाव इलेक्ट्रिक वाहनों से सस्ता है। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Heavy subsidies did not stop petrol and diesel cars from selling more, which shows that subsidy alone could not pull buyers fully towards EVs, so I follows<br>The statement says nothing about the cost of maintenance, so II rests on outside information and does not follow<br>Hence only inference I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Inference I follows..</b>","hi":"भारी सब्सिडी के बावजूद पेट्रोल तथा डीज़ल कारों की बिक्री बढ़ी, जिससे स्पष्ट है कि केवल सब्सिडी खरीदारों को पूरी तरह EV की ओर नहीं खींच सकी, अतः I निकलता है<br>कथन में रखरखाव की लागत के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहा गया, अतः II बाहरी जानकारी पर आधारित है और नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000071196","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line PQ, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba14-b91a-746d-aaf3-0f9f7687796e_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965788448\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि रेखा PQ पर दर्पण रखा जाए, तो प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिंब कौन-सी आकृति होगी?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019eba14-b91a-746d-aaf3-0f9f7687796e_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091309883\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22a37932073_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965831654\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea1-7297-9794-4ec3cbbad4b4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091342819\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"2":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22b3be7d153_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965881540\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71546bd5454b_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091380328\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"3":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22c225b2e40_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965924125\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71558fd4533b_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091410367\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"},"4":{"en":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22d91932e10_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965975280\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">","hi":"<img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71566497c723_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091447663\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The mirror stands on the vertical line PQ, so left and right interchange while up and down stay the same, and the word gJP93R written on the left appears on the right with every character turned horizontally and read from right to left<br>The mirror image must therefore begin with the flipped R, then 3, 9, P, J and end with the flipped g<br>Option C keeps some letters unflipped and options B and D change the order of the characters, so only the first option is the true mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22a37932073_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965831654\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण ऊर्ध्व रेखा PQ पर है, अतः बायाँ-दायाँ बदल जाता है और ऊपर-नीचे वही रहता है, तथा बाईं ओर लिखा gJP93R दाईं ओर प्रत्येक अक्षर के क्षैतिज रूप से पलटे होने पर दाएँ से बाएँ पढ़ा जाता है<br>अतः दर्पण प्रतिबिंब पलटे हुए R से शुरू होकर 3, 9, P, J तथा अंत में पलटे हुए g पर समाप्त होना चाहिए<br>विकल्प C में कुछ अक्षर नहीं पलटे हैं और विकल्प B तथा D क्रम बदल देते हैं, अतः केवल पहला विकल्प सही दर्पण प्रतिबिंब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea1-7297-9794-4ec3cbbad4b4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091342819\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba14-b91a-746d-aaf3-0f9f7687796e_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965788448","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019eba14-b91a-746d-aaf3-0f9f7687796e_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091309883"],"options":{"1":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22a37932073_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965831654","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea1-7297-9794-4ec3cbbad4b4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091342819"],"2":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22b3be7d153_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965881540","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71546bd5454b_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091380328"],"3":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22c225b2e40_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965924125","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71558fd4533b_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091410367"],"4":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22d91932e10_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965975280","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea2-7f31-86a7-71566497c723_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091447663"]},"solution":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019eba17-5b50-7472-ac80-b22a37932073_EN.jpg?edu=639294380965831654","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f26e8-aea1-7297-9794-4ec3cbbad4b4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091342819"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000071197","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">26</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">पंक्ति</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">21</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">20</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">26</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, IV तथा V"},"2":{"en":"Columns II, III and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, III तथा V"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, II तथा V"},"4":{"en":"Columns II, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ II, III तथा IV"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In column II the numbers are 21, 15, 18, 12 and 9 and in column V they are 14, 10, 12, 8 and 6, so every number of column V is two thirds of the number beside it in column II: 21 × 2/3 = 14 ✔ and 15 × 2/3 = 10 ✔<br>In column I the numbers are 7, 5, 6, 4 and 3, so column V is exactly double of column I: 7 × 2 = 14 ✔ and 5 × 2 = 10 ✔<br>Columns I, II and V are therefore linked by these fixed ratios, while columns III and IV do not follow the same relation<br>So columns I, II and V are related to each other<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Columns I, II and V.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ II में संख्याएँ 21, 15, 18, 12 तथा 9 हैं और स्तंभ V में 14, 10, 12, 8 तथा 6 हैं, अतः स्तंभ V की प्रत्येक संख्या स्तंभ II की बगल की संख्या की दो-तिहाई है: 21 × 2/3 = 14 ✔ तथा 15 × 2/3 = 10 ✔<br>स्तंभ I में संख्याएँ 7, 5, 6, 4 तथा 3 हैं, अतः स्तंभ V, स्तंभ I का ठीक दुगुना है: 7 × 2 = 14 ✔ तथा 5 × 2 = 10 ✔<br>अतः स्तंभ I, II तथा V इन निश्चित अनुपातों से जुड़े हैं, जबकि स्तंभ III तथा IV इसी संबंध का पालन नहीं करते<br>इसलिए स्तंभ I, II तथा V परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): स्तंभ I, II तथा V है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000071198","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Choose the image that does NOT belong to the group.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ede24-87dd-721a-bb5c-b6c6666a4a65_EN.jpg?edu=639294380966301283\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"वह आकृति चुनिए जो समूह से संबंधित नहीं है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ede24-87dd-721a-bb5c-b6c6666a4a65_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091701899\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In figures (A), (B) and (D) the outer shape is a trapezium with its wider side at the bottom, and the small circle inside carries a similar small mark at the same place<br>In figure (C) the trapezium is turned upside down with its wider side at the top, so the whole figure is inverted<br>Hence figure (C) does not belong to the group<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C.</b>","hi":"आकृति (A), (B) तथा (D) में बाहरी आकार समलंब है जिसकी चौड़ी भुजा नीचे है और भीतर का छोटा वृत्त एक ही स्थान पर समान चिह्न लिए है<br>आकृति (C) में समलंब उलटा है और उसकी चौड़ी भुजा ऊपर है, अर्थात् पूरी आकृति उलटी है<br>अतः आकृति (C) समूह से संबंधित नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ede24-87dd-721a-bb5c-b6c6666a4a65_EN.jpg?edu=639294380966301283","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ede24-87dd-721a-bb5c-b6c6666a4a65_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091701899"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000071199","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ef322-5a9a-7470-97ca-d4ca1c1a9e27_EN.jpg?edu=639294380966583506\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह विकल्प पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक वैसी ही अंतर्निहित है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ef322-5a9a-7470-97ca-d4ca1c1a9e27_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091901538\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a shield-like shape: a rectangle whose lower side ends in a downward point, drawn in the centre of a square<br>Option B shows this shield shape formed by the lines of the two triangles inside the square, with the pointed lower part clearly present<br>In options A, C and D the inner lines make triangles, diagonals or arrows and the shield outline is not formed<br>Hence the figure is embedded in option B<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): B.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) ढाल जैसी है: एक आयत जिसकी निचली भुजा नीचे की ओर नुकीली होती है, और यह वर्ग के मध्य में है<br>विकल्प B में वर्ग के भीतर दो त्रिभुजों की रेखाओं से यही ढाल आकार बनता है और निचला नुकीला भाग स्पष्ट है<br>विकल्प A, C तथा D में भीतरी रेखाएँ त्रिभुज, विकर्ण या तीर बनाती हैं और ढाल का ढाँचा नहीं बनता<br>अतः आकृति विकल्प B में अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): B है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ef322-5a9a-7470-97ca-d4ca1c1a9e27_EN.jpg?edu=639294380966583506","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ef322-5a9a-7470-97ca-d4ca1c1a9e27_HI.jpg?edu=639294381091901538"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000071200","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Passage: Organizational psychologists study how employees adjust their efforts based on perceived fairness. When employees feel their contributions outweigh their rewards, they often engage in \"work-to-rule\" behavior—meticulously fulfilling contractual duties while withholding voluntary effort. This behavioral shift is a calculated strategy to restore a sense of balance, rather than a reflection of personal capability or clinical exhaustion. An employee consistently meets but never exceeds minimum standards, arrives and leaves exactly on time, and avoids voluntary tasks, without violating any company policy.<br>Question: Based on the passage, the employee's behavior is best understood as: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गद्यांश: संगठनात्मक मनोवैज्ञानिक अध्ययन करते हैं कि कर्मचारी अपने प्रयासों को कथित निष्पक्षता के आधार पर कैसे समायोजित करते हैं। जब कर्मचारियों को लगता है कि उनका योगदान उनके पुरस्कारों से अधिक है, तो वे अक्सर \"कार्य-से-नियम\" व्यवहार अपनाते हैं—संविदात्मक कर्तव्यों को बारीकी से पूरा करते हैं और स्वैच्छिक प्रयास नहीं करते। यह व्यवहारिक बदलाव संतुलन बहाल करने की एक सुनियोजित रणनीति है, व्यक्तिगत क्षमता या नैदानिक थकावट का प्रतिबिंब नहीं। एक कर्मचारी लगातार न्यूनतम मानकों को पूरा करता है परंतु उससे अधिक कभी नहीं करता, ठीक समय पर आता-जाता है और स्वैच्छिक कार्यों से बचता है, बिना कंपनी की किसी नीति का उल्लंघन किए।<br>प्रश्न: गद्यांश के आधार पर कर्मचारी का व्यवहार सर्वोत्तम रूप से किस रूप में समझा जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A psychological manifestation of severe burnout requiring clinical intervention.","hi":"गंभीर थकावट की मनोवैज्ञानिक अभिव्यक्ति जिसके लिए नैदानिक हस्तक्षेप आवश्यक है।"},"2":{"en":"A strategic recalibration of effort in response to perceived inequity.","hi":"कथित असमानता के प्रति प्रतिक्रिया में प्रयास का सुनियोजित पुनर्संतुलन।"},"3":{"en":"A lack of intrinsic motivation driven by an introverted personality trait.","hi":"अंतर्मुखी व्यक्तित्व लक्षण से उत्पन्न आंतरिक प्रेरणा की कमी।"},"4":{"en":"A disciplinary infraction that should be addressed in a performance review.","hi":"अनुशासनात्मक उल्लंघन जिसे प्रदर्शन समीक्षा में संबोधित किया जाना चाहिए।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The passage states clearly that work-to-rule behaviour is a calculated strategy to restore balance when rewards feel smaller than contributions<br>It also says the shift is not a reflection of personal capability or clinical exhaustion, which rules out burnout, and the employee breaks no company policy, which rules out a disciplinary matter<br>So the behaviour is a strategic recalibration of effort in response to perceived inequity<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A strategic recalibration of effort in response to perceived inequity..</b>","hi":"गद्यांश स्पष्ट रूप से कहता है कि कार्य-से-नियम व्यवहार संतुलन बहाल करने की सुनियोजित रणनीति है, जब पुरस्कार योगदान से कम लगते हैं<br>यह भी कहा गया है कि यह बदलाव व्यक्तिगत क्षमता या नैदानिक थकावट का प्रतिबिंब नहीं है, जिससे थकावट वाला विकल्प हट जाता है, और कर्मचारी कोई नीति नहीं तोड़ता, जिससे अनुशासनात्मक विकल्प हट जाता है<br>अतः व्यवहार कथित असमानता के प्रति प्रयास का सुनियोजित पुनर्संतुलन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): कथित असमानता के प्रति प्रतिक्रिया में प्रयास का सुनियोजित पुनर्संतुलन। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000071201","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given situation carefully and consider all the relevant facts, conditions and constraints. Choose the option that represents the most appropriate, practical and logical decision based solely on the information provided.<br>A corporate venture fund accelerates green tech innovations under three parameters: The technology must reduce carbon output by at least 20%, must use scalable recycled materials and must have a commercial launch plan ready. A new enterprise presents a technology that reduces carbon emissions by 25% and uses recycled materials, but has not yet formulated a commercial launch plan.<br>What decision should the fund managers make? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई परिस्थिति को ध्यान से पढ़िए और सभी प्रासंगिक तथ्यों, शर्तों तथा बाधाओं पर विचार कीजिए। वह विकल्प चुनिए जो केवल दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त, व्यावहारिक तथा तार्किक निर्णय दर्शाता है।<br>एक कॉर्पोरेट वेंचर फंड हरित प्रौद्योगिकी नवाचारों को तीन मानदंडों पर आगे बढ़ाता है: प्रौद्योगिकी को कार्बन उत्सर्जन कम से कम 20% घटाना चाहिए, मापनीय पुनर्चक्रित सामग्री का उपयोग करना चाहिए तथा वाणिज्यिक लॉन्च योजना तैयार होनी चाहिए। एक नया उद्यम ऐसी प्रौद्योगिकी प्रस्तुत करता है जो कार्बन उत्सर्जन 25% घटाती है और पुनर्चक्रित सामग्री का उपयोग करती है, परंतु उसने वाणिज्यिक लॉन्च योजना अभी तैयार नहीं की है।<br>फंड के प्रबंधकों को क्या निर्णय लेना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The enterprise should be rejected for venture acceleration.","hi":"उद्यम को वेंचर त्वरण के लिए अस्वीकार कर दिया जाना चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"The enterprise should be selected for venture acceleration.","hi":"उद्यम को वेंचर त्वरण के लिए चुना जाना चाहिए।"},"3":{"en":"The application should be referred to the Managing Partner.","hi":"आवेदन प्रबंध भागीदार को भेजा जाना चाहिए।"},"4":{"en":"The data provided is inadequate to take a decision.","hi":"निर्णय लेने के लिए दिया गया डेटा अपर्याप्त है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The fund requires all three conditions to be met, and here the carbon reduction of 25% and the use of recycled materials are satisfied<br>The third condition of a ready commercial launch plan is not met, and the rules say nothing about referring such cases elsewhere<br>So the enterprise fails one mandatory parameter and the application must be rejected<br>Hence the enterprise should be rejected for venture acceleration<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The enterprise should be rejected for venture acceleration..</b>","hi":"फंड के लिए तीनों शर्तें पूरी होना आवश्यक है, और यहाँ 25% कार्बन कमी तथा पुनर्चक्रित सामग्री का उपयोग पूरा होता है<br>तैयार वाणिज्यिक लॉन्च योजना की तीसरी शर्त पूरी नहीं होती, और नियम ऐसे मामलों को कहीं और भेजने की बात नहीं कहते<br>अतः उद्यम एक अनिवार्य मानदंड में असफल है और आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाना चाहिए<br>इसलिए उद्यम को वेंचर त्वरण के लिए अस्वीकार कर देना चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): उद्यम को वेंचर त्वरण के लिए अस्वीकार कर दिया जाना चाहिए। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000071202","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which fundamental state of matter completes the sequence as temperature decreases?<br>Plasma &#8594; Gas &#8594; Liquid &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"तापमान घटने पर कौन-सी मूल अवस्था अनुक्रम को पूरा करती है?<br>Plasma &#8594; Gas &#8594; Liquid &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vapour","hi":"वाष्प"},"2":{"en":"Crystal","hi":"क्रिस्टल"},"3":{"en":"Ion","hi":"आयन"},"4":{"en":"Solid","hi":"ठोस"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"As temperature falls, plasma turns into gas, gas condenses into liquid and liquid freezes into solid<br>So the next state after liquid in this order is solid<br>Vapour is a form of gas, while crystal and ion are not fundamental states of matter<br>Hence the sequence is completed by solid<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Solid.</b>","hi":"तापमान घटने पर प्लाज़्मा गैस में बदलता है, गैस द्रव में संघनित होती है और द्रव ठोस में जम जाता है<br>अतः इस क्रम में द्रव के बाद अगली अवस्था ठोस है<br>वाष्प गैस का ही रूप है, जबकि क्रिस्टल और आयन मूल अवस्थाएँ नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए अनुक्रम ठोस से पूरा होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ठोस है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000071203","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Compare the figures carefully and pick the one that differs from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/01a00f62-3ca5-7f89-a3ab-d01c420529f4_EN.jpg?edu=639294380967933099\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृतियों की तुलना ध्यान से कीजिए और वह आकृति चुनिए जो अन्य से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/01a00f62-3ca5-7f89-a3ab-d01c420529f4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381092867842\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B"},"2":{"en":"A"},"3":{"en":"D"},"4":{"en":"C"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In figures (A), (B) and (D) the outer shape is divided into four equal parts and exactly one part is shaded dark<br>In figure (C) the outer shape is an oval divided into four parts in which the dark shading covers two halves of unequal open shape, so the proportion of shaded area and the shape of the outer figure both differ from the rest<br>Hence figure (C) is the one that differs from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): C.</b>","hi":"आकृति (A), (B) तथा (D) में बाहरी आकार चार बराबर भागों में विभाजित है और ठीक एक भाग गहरा छायांकित है<br>आकृति (C) में बाहरी आकार अंडाकार है जिसके चार भागों में छायांकन भिन्न अनुपात में है, अतः छायांकित क्षेत्र का अनुपात तथा बाहरी आकार दोनों शेष से भिन्न हैं<br>इसलिए आकृति (C) अन्य से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/01a00f62-3ca5-7f89-a3ab-d01c420529f4_EN.jpg?edu=639294380967933099","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/01a00f62-3ca5-7f89-a3ab-d01c420529f4_HI.jpg?edu=639294381092867842"]}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000071204","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Which of the following fractions is the odd one out?<br>\\(\\frac{5}{11}\\), \\(\\frac{7}{15}\\), \\(\\frac{9}{19}\\), \\(\\frac{11}{24}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी भिन्न विषम है?<br>\\(\\frac{5}{11}\\), \\(\\frac{7}{15}\\), \\(\\frac{9}{19}\\), \\(\\frac{11}{24}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{11}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{7}{15}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{9}{19}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{11}{24}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first three fractions the denominator is the numerator plus 6: 5 + 6 = 11 ✔, 7 + 6 = 15 ✔ and 9 + 6 = 19 ✔<br>In the fourth fraction 11 + 6 = 17, but the denominator is 24 ✘<br>So the fourth fraction is the odd one out<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{11}{24}\\).</b>","hi":"पहली तीन भिन्नों में हर अंश से 6 अधिक है: 5 + 6 = 11 ✔, 7 + 6 = 15 ✔ तथा 9 + 6 = 19 ✔<br>चौथी भिन्न में 11 + 6 = 17 है, परंतु हर 24 है ✘<br>अतः चौथी भिन्न विषम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{11}{24}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000071205","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"Identify which of the four options correctly shows the pattern after the transparent sheet is folded along the dotted line.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/01a03796-fe26-72c2-bfaa-9ab0c0ba94b1_EN.jpg?edu=639294380968642299\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पारदर्शी शीट को बिंदुदार रेखा के अनुदिश मोड़ने पर बनने वाला पैटर्न चार विकल्पों में से कौन-सा सही दर्शाता है, पहचानिए।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/01a03796-fe26-72c2-bfaa-9ab0c0ba94b1_HI.jpg?edu=639294381093412246\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3] [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A"},"2":{"en":"B"},"3":{"en":"C"},"4":{"en":"D"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The dotted fold line is horizontal and lies just above the centre of the diamond, so the upper part of the sheet folds down on the lower part<br>The small circle with the arrow mark that lies above the fold line is seen through the sheet below the line as a mirrored copy, and the parts lying on the line are shared<br>Option A keeps the original upper circle in its old place, while options B and C join the two small circles into a single tangled mark<br>Only option D shows the diamond below the fold with the two small marks kept separate and the arrow pointing up, so the pattern is correct in option 4<br>Hence the fourth option is correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): D.</b>","hi":"बिंदुदार मोड़ रेखा क्षैतिज है और समचतुर्भुज के केंद्र से थोड़ा ऊपर है, अतः शीट का ऊपरी भाग निचले भाग पर मुड़ जाता है<br>मोड़ रेखा के ऊपर स्थित छोटा वृत्त अपने तीर चिह्न के साथ शीट के भीतर से रेखा के नीचे दर्पण रूप में दिखाई देता है, तथा रेखा पर पड़ा भाग साझा रहता है<br>विकल्प A मूल ऊपरी वृत्त को उसी स्थान पर रखता है, जबकि विकल्प B और C दोनों छोटे वृत्तों को एक उलझे चिह्न में मिला देते हैं<br>केवल विकल्प D में मोड़ के नीचे समचतुर्भुज तथा दोनों छोटे चिह्न अलग-अलग हैं, अतः पैटर्न विकल्प 4 में सही है<br>इसलिए चौथा विकल्प सही है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): D है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/01a03796-fe26-72c2-bfaa-9ab0c0ba94b1_EN.jpg?edu=639294380968642299","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/01a03796-fe26-72c2-bfaa-9ab0c0ba94b1_HI.jpg?edu=639294381093412246"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000071206","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: India and Its Location","question":{"en":"The Union Territory of Puducherry (Pondicherry) has its territories spread across which of the following states? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पुदुच्चेरी (पांडिचेरी) केंद्रशासित प्रदेश के क्षेत्र निम्नलिखित में से किन राज्यों में फैले हैं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, and Maharashtra","hi":"तमिलनाडु, आंध्र प्रदेश तथा महाराष्ट्र"},"2":{"en":"Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, and Kerala","hi":"तमिलनाडु, कर्नाटक तथा केरल"},"3":{"en":"Tamil Nadu, Kerala, and Andhra Pradesh","hi":"तमिलनाडु, केरल तथा आंध्र प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Tamil Nadu, Karnataka, and Goa","hi":"तमिलनाडु, कर्नाटक तथा गोवा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Tamil Nadu, Kerala, and Andhra Pradesh</b><br>The Union Territory of <b>Puducherry</b> consists of four non-contiguous regions – <b>Puducherry and Karaikal</b> in Tamil Nadu, <b>Mahe</b> in Kerala and <b>Yanam</b> in Andhra Pradesh.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>de jure transfer</b> of the French settlements took place in 1962, and Puducherry became a Union Territory with a legislature under the Government of Union Territories Act, 1963.<br>• <b>Yanam</b> lies on the Godavari delta in Andhra Pradesh, <b>Mahe</b> is on the west coast near Kannur in Kerala and <b>Karaikal</b> is south of Puducherry.<br>• Puducherry is the only Union Territory (apart from Delhi and Jammu and Kashmir) with a Legislative Assembly and a Council of Ministers.<br>• Puducherry is bounded by the Bay of Bengal and the states of Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Andhra Pradesh only.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Puducherry's territories lie in Tamil Nadu, Kerala and Andhra Pradesh.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – तमिलनाडु, केरल तथा आंध्र प्रदेश</b><br><b>पुदुच्चेरी</b> केंद्रशासित प्रदेश में चार असंलग्न क्षेत्र हैं – तमिलनाडु में <b>पुदुच्चेरी तथा कराईकल</b>, केरल में <b>माहे</b> तथा आंध्र प्रदेश में <b>यनम</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• फ्रांसीसी बस्तियों का <b>विधिक हस्तांतरण</b> 1962 में हुआ, और पुदुच्चेरी संघ राज्यक्षेत्र अधिनियम, 1963 के अंतर्गत विधान सभा वाला केंद्रशासित प्रदेश बना।<br>• <b>यनम</b> आंध्र प्रदेश में गोदावरी डेल्टा पर, <b>माहे</b> केरल में कन्नूर के निकट पश्चिमी तट पर तथा <b>कराईकल</b> पुदुच्चेरी के दक्षिण में स्थित है।<br>• पुदुच्चेरी (दिल्ली तथा जम्मू-कश्मीर के अतिरिक्त) एकमात्र केंद्रशासित प्रदेश है जिसकी विधान सभा तथा मंत्रिपरिषद है।<br>• पुदुच्चेरी बंगाल की खाड़ी तथा केवल तमिलनाडु, केरल एवं आंध्र प्रदेश राज्यों से घिरा है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पुदुच्चेरी के क्षेत्र तमिलनाडु, केरल तथा आंध्र प्रदेश में हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000071207","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Rapeseed and mustard are grown in: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"राई (सरसों) तथा सरसों की फसल उगाई जाती है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"April - June","hi":"अप्रैल - जून"},"2":{"en":"June - September","hi":"जून - सितंबर"},"3":{"en":"October - March","hi":"अक्टूबर - मार्च"},"4":{"en":"April - August","hi":"अप्रैल - अगस्त"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – October - March</b><br><b>Rapeseed and mustard</b> are <b>rabi</b> crops, sown in <b>October-December</b> and harvested in <b>February-March</b>, and India is one of the world's largest producers of rapeseed-mustard.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Major producers are <b>Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh and Gujarat</b>, and it is the main source of edible oil in north and central India.<br>• The crop needs a <b>cool, dry growing season</b> and about 25-45 cm of rainfall, and it is largely grown on rainfed and conserved-moisture land.<br>• The April-June period is the <b>zaid</b> season and June-September the <b>kharif</b> season, during which mustard is not grown.<br>• Mustard oil cake is also used as cattle feed and fertiliser, and 'Pusa Mustard' is a popular variety series.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because rapeseed and mustard are grown from October to March.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अक्टूबर - मार्च</b><br><b>राई तथा सरसों</b> <b>रबी</b> की फसलें हैं, जिनकी बुवाई <b>अक्टूबर-दिसंबर</b> में तथा कटाई <b>फरवरी-मार्च</b> में होती है, और भारत विश्व के सबसे बड़े राई-सरसों उत्पादकों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रमुख उत्पादक राज्य <b>राजस्थान, मध्य प्रदेश, हरियाणा, उत्तर प्रदेश तथा गुजरात</b> हैं, और यह उत्तर एवं मध्य भारत में खाद्य तेल का मुख्य स्रोत है।<br>• इस फसल को <b>ठंडा एवं शुष्क बढ़वार मौसम</b> तथा लगभग 25-45 सेमी वर्षा चाहिए, और यह मुख्यतः वर्षा-आधारित एवं संरक्षित नमी वाली भूमि पर उगाई जाती है।<br>• अप्रैल-जून <b>ज़ायद</b> मौसम तथा जून-सितंबर <b>खरीफ</b> मौसम है, जिनमें सरसों नहीं उगाई जाती।<br>• सरसों की खली पशु आहार तथा उर्वरक के रूप में भी प्रयुक्त होती है, और 'पूसा सरसों' किस्मों की लोकप्रिय श्रृंखला है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि राई तथा सरसों अक्टूबर से मार्च तक उगाई जाती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000071208","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which category of substances under the World Anti-Doping Code is more likely to have a credible non-doping explanation? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"विश्व डोप-रोधी संहिता के अंतर्गत पदार्थों की किस श्रेणी के लिए गैर-डोपिंग स्पष्टीकरण की विश्वसनीय संभावना अधिक होती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Non-specified","hi":"अनिर्दिष्ट (Non-specified)"},"2":{"en":"Specified","hi":"निर्दिष्ट (Specified)"},"3":{"en":"Prohibited","hi":"निषिद्ध (Prohibited)"},"4":{"en":"Natural","hi":"प्राकृतिक (Natural)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Specified</b><br>Under the <b>World Anti-Doping Code</b>, <b>Specified substances</b> are those more likely to have a <b>credible non-doping explanation</b>, because they may be present through contamination, food or medication, and therefore attract lighter sanctions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The WADA Prohibited List classifies substances as <b>Specified or Non-specified</b>, and non-specified substances are usually those used deliberately for performance enhancement, with tougher sanctions.<br>• For a specified substance, an athlete can establish <b>no significant fault or negligence</b> more easily, leading to a reduced period of ineligibility.<br>• The Prohibited List is published by <b>WADA</b> and is updated annually, and it covers substances and methods prohibited in and out of competition.<br>• 'Prohibited' is the general term for the list, not a separate class, and 'natural' is not a classification under the Code.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because specified substances are more likely to have a non-doping explanation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – निर्दिष्ट (Specified)</b><br><b>विश्व डोप-रोधी संहिता</b> के अंतर्गत <b>निर्दिष्ट पदार्थ</b> वे होते हैं जिनके लिए <b>डोपिंग-रहित विश्वसनीय स्पष्टीकरण की संभावना अधिक</b> होती है, क्योंकि वे संदूषण, भोजन या दवा के माध्यम से शरीर में पहुँच सकते हैं, और इसलिए उन पर हल्के दंड लगते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• WADA की निषिद्ध सूची पदार्थों को <b>निर्दिष्ट या अनिर्दिष्ट</b> में वर्गीकृत करती है; अनिर्दिष्ट पदार्थ सामान्यतः प्रदर्शन बढ़ाने हेतु जानबूझकर लिए जाते हैं और उन पर कठोर दंड होते हैं।<br>• निर्दिष्ट पदार्थ के मामले में खिलाड़ी <b>कोई महत्वपूर्ण त्रुटि या लापरवाही नहीं</b> सिद्ध करना अधिक आसानी से सिद्ध कर सकता है, जिससे निरर्हता की अवधि घट जाती है।<br>• निषिद्ध सूची <b>WADA</b> प्रकाशित करता है और यह प्रतिवर्ष अद्यतन होती है; इसमें प्रतियोगिता के दौरान तथा बाहर निषिद्ध पदार्थ एवं विधियाँ सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• 'निषिद्ध' सूची का सामान्य नाम है, पृथक वर्ग नहीं, और 'प्राकृतिक' संहिता के अंतर्गत कोई वर्गीकरण नहीं है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि निर्दिष्ट पदार्थों के लिए डोपिंग-रहित स्पष्टीकरण की संभावना अधिक होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000071209","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In football, what is the standard length of a \"penalty mark\" from the goal line? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"फुटबॉल में गोल लाइन से 'पेनल्टी मार्क' की मानक दूरी कितनी है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11 meters (12 yards)","hi":"11 मीटर (12 गज)"},"2":{"en":"10 meters (11 yards)","hi":"10 मीटर (11 गज)"},"3":{"en":"9.15 meters (10.5 yards)","hi":"9.15 मीटर (10.5 गज)"},"4":{"en":"12 meters (13 yards)","hi":"12 मीटर (13 गज)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 11 meters (12 yards)</b><br>In football the <b>penalty mark</b> is placed <b>11 metres (12 yards)</b> from the goal line, along the perpendicular bisector of the goal, and the penalty area extends 16.5 metres (18 yards) from the goalposts.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The penalty arc outside the penalty area is drawn at a radius of <b>9.15 metres (10 yards)</b> from the penalty mark.<br>• A penalty kick is awarded for a direct free-kick offence inside the penalty area, and the goalkeeper must keep both feet on the goal line at the moment of the kick.<br>• Other standard measurements are the <b>goal 7.32 m wide and 2.44 m high</b> and the centre circle radius of 9.15 m.<br>• Football is played for <b>90 minutes</b> in two halves of 45 minutes, with 11 players per side.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the penalty mark is 11 metres from the goal line.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 11 मीटर (12 गज)</b><br>फुटबॉल में <b>पेनल्टी मार्क</b> गोल लाइन से <b>11 मीटर (12 गज)</b> की दूरी पर, गोल के लंब समद्विभाजक पर होता है, तथा पेनल्टी क्षेत्र गोलपोस्ट से 16.5 मीटर (18 गज) तक फैला होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पेनल्टी क्षेत्र के बाहर का पेनल्टी चाप पेनल्टी मार्क से <b>9.15 मीटर (10 गज)</b> की त्रिज्या पर बनाया जाता है।<br>• पेनल्टी क्षेत्र के भीतर प्रत्यक्ष फ्री-किक अपराध पर पेनल्टी किक मिलती है, और किक के समय गोलकीपर के दोनों पैर गोल लाइन पर होने चाहिए।<br>• अन्य मानक माप हैं – <b>गोल की चौड़ाई 7.32 मीटर तथा ऊँचाई 2.44 मीटर</b>, और मध्य वृत्त की त्रिज्या 9.15 मीटर।<br>• फुटबॉल <b>90 मिनट</b> तक 45-45 मिनट के दो हाफ में खेला जाता है, प्रत्येक पक्ष में 11 खिलाड़ी होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि पेनल्टी मार्क गोल लाइन से 11 मीटर पर होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000071210","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In the inaugural Kho-Kho World Cup 2025, which country emerged as the Men's Champion? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"प्रथम खो-खो विश्व कप 2025 में पुरुष वर्ग का विजेता कौन-सा देश बना? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"2":{"en":"India","hi":"भारत"},"3":{"en":"Bangladesh","hi":"बांग्लादेश"},"4":{"en":"Sri Lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – India</b><br>In the <b>inaugural Kho-Kho World Cup 2025</b>, held at the <b>Indira Gandhi Indoor Stadium in New Delhi</b> in January 2025, <b>India</b> won the <b>men's title</b> by defeating Nepal in the final.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India also won the <b>women's title</b> in the same tournament by defeating Nepal, completing a double.<br>• The World Cup was organised by the <b>Kho Kho Federation of India</b> with the International Kho Kho Federation, and 20 men's and 19 women's teams took part.<br>• The mascot of the tournament was 'Tejas', and the event was supported by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports.<br>• Nepal finished as runners-up in both finals, and Bangladesh and Sri Lanka were among the other participating teams.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because India won the men's title in the inaugural Kho-Kho World Cup 2025.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत</b><br>जनवरी 2025 में <b>नई दिल्ली के इंदिरा गांधी इंडोर स्टेडियम</b> में हुए <b>प्रथम खो-खो विश्व कप 2025</b> में <b>भारत</b> ने फाइनल में नेपाल को हराकर <b>पुरुष वर्ग का खिताब</b> जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत ने इसी टूर्नामेंट में नेपाल को हराकर <b>महिला वर्ग का खिताब</b> भी जीता और दोहरा सफलता प्राप्त की।<br>• विश्व कप का आयोजन <b>खो-खो फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया</b> ने अंतरराष्ट्रीय खो-खो महासंघ के साथ किया, जिसमें पुरुषों की 20 तथा महिलाओं की 19 टीमों ने भाग लिया।<br>• टूर्नामेंट का शुभंकर 'तेजस' था, और आयोजन को युवा कार्यक्रम एवं खेल मंत्रालय का समर्थन प्राप्त था।<br>• दोनों फाइनल में नेपाल उपविजेता रहा, तथा बांग्लादेश एवं श्रीलंका अन्य भागीदार टीमों में थे।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि प्रथम खो-खो विश्व कप 2025 में भारत ने पुरुष वर्ग का खिताब जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000071211","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Constitutional and Non-Constitutional Bodies","question":{"en":"Which constitutional authority in India is referred to as the “guardian of the public purse”? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में किस संवैधानिक प्राधिकारी को \"लोक कोष का संरक्षक\" कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Finance Secretary","hi":"वित्त सचिव"},"2":{"en":"Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG)","hi":"नियंत्रक एवं महालेखापरीक्षक (CAG)"},"3":{"en":"Governor of Reserve Bank of India (RBI)","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक (RBI) के गवर्नर"},"4":{"en":"Attorney General of India (AG)","hi":"भारत के महान्यायवादी (AG)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG)</b><br>The <b>Comptroller and Auditor General of India</b> is described as the <b>'guardian of the public purse'</b> because it audits all receipts and expenditure of the Union and the states and reports to Parliament.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The CAG is appointed under <b>Article 148</b>, holds office for six years or up to 65 years of age and can be removed only in the manner of a Supreme Court judge.<br>• The CAG is the <b>head of the Indian Audit and Accounts Department</b> and audits government companies and corporations too.<br>• The <b>Finance Secretary</b> heads the Finance Ministry's bureaucracy, the <b>RBI Governor</b> manages monetary policy and the <b>Attorney General</b> is the chief legal adviser to the government.<br>• Dr B.R. Ambedkar described the CAG as the <b>most important officer under the Constitution</b> for financial control over the executive.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the CAG is known as the guardian of the public purse.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – नियंत्रक एवं महालेखापरीक्षक (CAG)</b><br><b>भारत के नियंत्रक एवं महालेखापरीक्षक</b> को <b>'लोक कोष का संरक्षक'</b> कहा जाता है, क्योंकि वह संघ तथा राज्यों की समस्त प्राप्तियों एवं व्ययों का लेखापरीक्षण करके संसद को प्रतिवेदन देता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CAG की नियुक्ति <b>अनुच्छेद 148</b> के अंतर्गत होती है, कार्यकाल छह वर्ष या 65 वर्ष की आयु तक होता है और उसे सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीश की रीति से ही हटाया जा सकता है।<br>• CAG <b>भारतीय लेखापरीक्षा एवं लेखा विभाग का प्रमुख</b> है और सरकारी कंपनियों तथा निगमों का भी लेखापरीक्षण करता है।<br>• <b>वित्त सचिव</b> वित्त मंत्रालय के अधिकारीतंत्र का प्रमुख है, <b>RBI गवर्नर</b> मौद्रिक नीति संभालता है और <b>महान्यायवादी</b> सरकार का मुख्य विधि सलाहकार है।<br>• डॉ. बी. आर. आंबेडकर ने CAG को कार्यपालिका पर वित्तीय नियंत्रण हेतु <b>संविधान के अंतर्गत सबसे महत्वपूर्ण अधिकारी</b> कहा।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि CAG लोक कोष का संरक्षक कहलाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000071212","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In weightlifting, if three red lights appear after a lift, it indicates: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारोत्तोलन में यदि किसी उठान के बाद तीन लाल प्रकाश दिखाई दें तो इसका अर्थ है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Record attempt","hi":"रिकॉर्ड प्रयास"},"2":{"en":"Disqualification","hi":"निरर्हता"},"3":{"en":"Unsuccessful lift","hi":"असफल उठान"},"4":{"en":"Reattempt allowed","hi":"पुनः प्रयास की अनुमति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Unsuccessful lift</b><br>In weightlifting, <b>three red lights</b> from the referees mean the lift is <b>unsuccessful</b>, while white lights indicate a good lift; a lift needs at least <b>two white lights</b> to be valid.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Three referees judge each attempt, and <b>red denotes a fault</b> such as pressing out with the arms, uneven extension or the barbell touching the platform.<br>• In Olympic lifting the <b>snatch and clean and jerk</b> are contested, with three attempts in each lift.<br>• The jury may override a decision after video review in case of referee error.<br>• A lift is not a disqualification of the athlete for the whole event, and a reattempt is allowed only as part of the normal three attempts.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because three red lights mean the lift is unsuccessful.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – असफल उठान</b><br>भारोत्तोलन में रेफरियों के <b>तीन लाल प्रकाश</b> का अर्थ होता है कि उठान <b>असफल</b> है, जबकि श्वेत प्रकाश अच्छी उठान दर्शाता है; वैध उठान के लिए कम से कम <b>दो श्वेत प्रकाश</b> आवश्यक हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रत्येक प्रयास को तीन रेफरी आँकते हैं, और <b>लाल दोष</b> दर्शाता है, जैसे हाथों से प्रेस करना, असमान विस्तार या बारबेल का प्लेटफॉर्म को छूना।<br>• ओलंपिक उठानों में <b>स्नैच तथा क्लीन एंड जर्क</b> होते हैं, प्रत्येक में तीन प्रयास।<br>• रेफरी की त्रुटि पर ज्यूरी वीडियो समीक्षा के बाद निर्णय बदल सकती है।<br>• उठान असफल होना पूरे इवेंट से खिलाड़ी की निरर्हता नहीं है, और पुनः प्रयास केवल सामान्य तीन प्रयासों के अंतर्गत मिलता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि तीन लाल प्रकाश असफल उठान दर्शाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000071213","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Consider the following pairs of musicians and their associated instruments:<br>1. T. R. Mahalingam – Flute<br>2. Lalgudi Jayaram – Violin<br>Which of the pairs given above is/are <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"संगीतकारों तथा उनसे संबंधित वाद्यों के निम्नलिखित युग्मों पर विचार करें:<br>1. टी. आर. महालिंगम – बाँसुरी<br>2. लालगुडी जयराम – वायलिन<br>इनमें से कौन-सा/से युग्म <b>सही</b> मेल खाता/खाते है/हैं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 तथा 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न तो 1 न ही 2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Both 1 and 2</b><br>Both pairs are correctly matched – <b>T.R. Mahalingam</b> was a legendary <b>Carnatic flautist</b>, and <b>Lalgudi Jayaraman</b> was a celebrated <b>Carnatic violinist</b> and composer.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• T.R. Mahalingam, known as <b>'Flute Mali'</b>, revolutionised the Carnatic flute with his fingering technique and was awarded the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award.<br>• Lalgudi Jayaraman was famous for the <b>'Lalgudi bani'</b> of violin playing and composed the 'Lalgudi Pancharatna' and varnams.<br>• Other Carnatic instrumentalists include <b>M.S. Gopalakrishnan (violin), N. Ramani (flute) and U. Srinivas (mandolin)</b>.<br>• Hindustani counterparts include <b>Hariprasad Chaurasia (flute) and Pandit Ravi Shankar (sitar)</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because both the musician-instrument pairs are correctly matched.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1 तथा 2 दोनों</b><br>दोनों युग्म सही मेल खाते हैं – <b>टी. आर. महालिंगम</b> प्रसिद्ध <b>कर्नाटक बाँसुरी वादक</b> थे तथा <b>लालगुडी जयराम</b> प्रतिष्ठित <b>कर्नाटक वायलिन वादक</b> एवं संगीतकार थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टी. आर. महालिंगम, जिन्हें <b>'फ्लूट माली'</b> कहा जाता था, अपनी उँगली-तकनीक से कर्नाटक बाँसुरी में क्रांति लाए और उन्हें संगीत नाटक अकादमी पुरस्कार मिला।<br>• लालगुडी जयराम वायलिन वादन की <b>'लालगुडी बानी'</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध थे और उन्होंने 'लालगुडी पंचरत्न' तथा वर्णम रचे।<br>• अन्य कर्नाटक वादकों में <b>एम. एस. गोपालकृष्णन (वायलिन), एन. रामणी (बाँसुरी) तथा यू. श्रीनिवास (मैंडोलिन)</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• हिंदुस्तानी परंपरा में <b>हरिप्रसाद चौरसिया (बाँसुरी) तथा पंडित रविशंकर (सितार)</b> प्रमुख हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि संगीतकार-वाद्य के दोनों युग्म सही मेल खाते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000071214","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the purpose of the Platform Aggregator Module launched on the e-Shram portal? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"ई-श्रम पोर्टल पर शुरू किए गए प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटर मॉड्यूल का उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A tool to aggregate crop prices","hi":"फसल कीमतों को एकत्र करने का उपकरण"},"2":{"en":"A module for registering platform aggregators","hi":"प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटरों के पंजीकरण का मॉड्यूल"},"3":{"en":"A system to aggregate voter lists","hi":"मतदाता सूचियों को एकत्र करने की प्रणाली"},"4":{"en":"A tool for bank loans","hi":"बैंक ऋण हेतु उपकरण"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – A module for registering platform aggregators</b><br>The <b>Platform Aggregator Module</b> on the <b>e-Shram portal</b> enables <b>platform aggregators</b> such as food-delivery and ride-hailing companies to <b>register themselves</b> and their gig workers, helping extend social security benefits to platform workers.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>e-Shram</b>, launched in 2021, is the national database of unorganised workers maintained by the Ministry of Labour and Employment.<br>• The Budget 2025-26 announced the extension of <b>AB-PMJAY healthcare cover</b> to gig workers, and the module helps identify and onboard them.<br>• Registered workers get an e-Shram card with a Universal Account Number (UAN) and accident insurance cover under the <b>Pradhan Mantri Suraksha Bima Yojana</b>.<br>• The Code on Social Security, 2020 defines gig workers and platform workers and provides for a <b>Social Security Fund</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the module is meant for registering platform aggregators.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटरों के पंजीकरण का मॉड्यूल</b><br><b>ई-श्रम पोर्टल</b> पर <b>प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटर मॉड्यूल</b> खाद्य-वितरण तथा राइड-हेलिंग कंपनियों जैसे <b>प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटरों</b> को स्वयं तथा अपने गिग श्रमिकों को <b>पंजीकृत</b> करने की सुविधा देता है, जिससे प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिकों तक सामाजिक सुरक्षा लाभ बढ़ते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2021 में शुरू <b>ई-श्रम</b> असंगठित श्रमिकों का राष्ट्रीय डेटाबेस है, जिसे श्रम एवं रोजगार मंत्रालय संभालता है।<br>• बजट 2025-26 में गिग श्रमिकों तक <b>AB-PMJAY स्वास्थ्य कवर</b> बढ़ाने की घोषणा हुई, और यह मॉड्यूल उनकी पहचान एवं पंजीकरण में सहायक है।<br>• पंजीकृत श्रमिकों को सार्वभौमिक खाता संख्या (UAN) युक्त ई-श्रम कार्ड तथा <b>प्रधानमंत्री सुरक्षा बीमा योजना</b> के अंतर्गत दुर्घटना बीमा मिलता है।<br>• सामाजिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2020 गिग तथा प्लेटफॉर्म श्रमिकों को परिभाषित करती है और <b>सामाजिक सुरक्षा कोष</b> का प्रावधान करती है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि यह मॉड्यूल प्लेटफॉर्म एग्रीगेटरों के पंजीकरण के लिए है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000071215","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Thimphu is the capital of: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"थिम्पू किसकी राजधानी है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sri Lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"},"2":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"3":{"en":"Maldives","hi":"मालदीव"},"4":{"en":"Bhutan","hi":"भूटान"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Bhutan</b><br><b>Thimphu</b> is the capital and largest city of <b>Bhutan</b>, located in the western part of the country on the Wang Chhu river.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bhutan's capitals in history included <b>Punakha</b> and <b>Paro</b> before Thimphu became the permanent capital in 1955.<br>• Thimphu is the only capital city in the world without traffic lights and is home to the <b>Tashichho Dzong</b>, the seat of government.<br>• Bhutan is a Himalayan kingdom bordered by <b>India, China and Tibet</b>, and its currency is the ngultrum.<br>• <b>Sri Lanka's</b> capital is Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte (Colombo is the commercial capital), <b>Nepal's</b> is Kathmandu and the <b>Maldives'</b> is Male.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because Thimphu is the capital of Bhutan.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – भूटान</b><br><b>थिम्पू</b> <b>भूटान</b> की राजधानी तथा सबसे बड़ा नगर है, जो देश के पश्चिमी भाग में वांग छू नदी पर स्थित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1955 में थिम्पू के स्थायी राजधानी बनने से पहले भूटान की राजधानियों में <b>पुनाखा</b> तथा <b>पारो</b> रहे थे।<br>• थिम्पू विश्व की एकमात्र ऐसी राजधानी है जहाँ ट्रैफिक लाइट नहीं है, और यहाँ सरकार का केंद्र <b>ताशिचो द्जोंग</b> स्थित है।<br>• भूटान हिमालयी राज्य है, जो <b>भारत, चीन तथा तिब्बत</b> से घिरा है, और उसकी मुद्रा न्गुलत्रुम है।<br>• <b>श्रीलंका</b> की राजधानी श्री जयवर्धनेपुरा कोट्टे (कोलंबो वाणिज्यिक राजधानी), <b>नेपाल</b> की काठमांडू तथा <b>मालदीव</b> की माले है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि थिम्पू भूटान की राजधानी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000071216","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"The South Asian country which is the newest entrant to South Asian Association for Regional Cooperation (SAARC) is: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सार्क (दक्षिण एशियाई क्षेत्रीय सहयोग संगठन) में नवीनतम रूप से सम्मिलित दक्षिण एशियाई देश है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Afghanistan","hi":"अफगानिस्तान"},"2":{"en":"Maldives","hi":"मालदीव"},"3":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"4":{"en":"Bhutan","hi":"भूटान"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Afghanistan</b><br><b>Afghanistan</b> is the newest member of <b>SAARC</b>, having joined as its <b>eighth member in 2007</b> at the 14th SAARC Summit held in New Delhi.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• SAARC was founded on <b>8 December 1985</b> at Dhaka by Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan and Sri Lanka, with its secretariat at <b>Kathmandu</b>.<br>• The eight member states are <b>Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Bhutan, India, Maldives, Nepal, Pakistan and Sri Lanka</b>.<br>• SAARC's principles include <b>sovereign equality, territorial integrity and non-interference</b>, and its summits are held biennially.<br>• SAARC has observer status for countries such as China, Japan, the USA and the European Union, and has free trade arrangements through <b>SAFTA</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Afghanistan is the newest SAARC member.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अफगानिस्तान</b><br><b>अफगानिस्तान</b> <b>सार्क</b> का नवीनतम सदस्य है, जो नई दिल्ली में हुए 14वें सार्क शिखर सम्मेलन में <b>2007 में आठवें सदस्य</b> के रूप में शामिल हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सार्क की स्थापना <b>8 दिसंबर 1985</b> को ढाका में बांग्लादेश, भूटान, भारत, मालदीव, नेपाल, पाकिस्तान तथा श्रीलंका द्वारा हुई, और इसका सचिवालय <b>काठमांडू</b> में है।<br>• इसके आठ सदस्य देश <b>अफगानिस्तान, बांग्लादेश, भूटान, भारत, मालदीव, नेपाल, पाकिस्तान तथा श्रीलंका</b> हैं।<br>• सार्क के सिद्धांतों में <b>संप्रभु समता, क्षेत्रीय अखंडता तथा अहस्तक्षेप</b> सम्मिलित हैं, और इसके शिखर सम्मेलन द्विवार्षिक होते हैं।<br>• चीन, जापान, अमेरिका तथा यूरोपीय संघ जैसे देशों को सार्क में प्रेक्षक का दर्जा है, और <b>SAFTA</b> के माध्यम से मुक्त व्यापार व्यवस्था है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि अफगानिस्तान सार्क का नवीनतम सदस्य है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000071217","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"In a dispute over whether villagers have a right to use a pond, the court considers the following:<br>(i) testimony of elderly villagers<br>(ii) written government notification denying such right<br>Which is legally correct under Section 42 of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023, in India? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गाँव के लोगों के तालाब का उपयोग करने के अधिकार पर विवाद में न्यायालय निम्नलिखित पर विचार करता है:<br>(i) वृद्ध ग्रामीणों का साक्ष्य<br>(ii) ऐसे अधिकार से इनकार करने वाला लिखित सरकारी अधिसूचना<br>भारत में भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 की धारा 42 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only government notification is relevant.","hi":"केवल सरकारी अधिसूचना सुसंगत है।"},"2":{"en":"Only elderly villagers’ opinions are relevant.","hi":"केवल वृद्ध ग्रामीणों की राय सुसंगत है।"},"3":{"en":"Both are irrelevant because customs cannot be proved by opinion.","hi":"दोनों असुसंगत हैं क्योंकि रीति-रिवाज राय से सिद्ध नहीं किए जा सकते।"},"4":{"en":"Elderly villagers’ opinions are relevant as they likely know the custom.","hi":"वृद्ध ग्रामीणों की राय सुसंगत है क्योंकि वे संभवतः रीति-रिवाज जानते हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Elderly villagers’ opinions are relevant as they likely know the custom.</b><br>Under <b>Section 42 of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> (corresponding to Section 32 of the old Evidence Act), when a court has to form an opinion on a <b>point of general custom or right</b>, the <b>opinions of persons likely to know of its existence</b>, such as elderly villagers, are relevant.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The section covers customs and rights common to a class of persons, a community or a family, such as rights of way, village grazing and pond-use rights.<br>• Opinion evidence is an <b>exception to the rule that witnesses state facts, not opinions</b>.<br>• The government notification denying the right is a <b>documentary fact</b> that may also be relevant, but the question asks about the relevance under Section 42, which deals with opinion on custom.<br>• Similar provisions cover opinions of <b>experts (Section 39) and handwriting comparison</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the opinions of elderly villagers who know the custom are relevant.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – वृद्ध ग्रामीणों की राय सुसंगत है क्योंकि वे संभवतः रीति-रिवाज जानते हैं।</b><br><b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 की धारा 42</b> (पुराने साक्ष्य अधिनियम की धारा 32 के समान) के अंतर्गत जब न्यायालय को <b>सामान्य रीति-रिवाज या अधिकार के बिंदु</b> पर राय बनानी हो, तो <b>उन व्यक्तियों की राय सुसंगत है जो उसके अस्तित्व को जानने योग्य हैं</b>, जैसे वृद्ध ग्रामीण।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह धारा व्यक्तियों के वर्ग, समुदाय या परिवार के सामान्य रीति-रिवाजों एवं अधिकारों पर लागू होती है, जैसे रास्ते का अधिकार, गाँव की चराई तथा तालाब-उपयोग का अधिकार।<br>• राय-साक्ष्य उस नियम का <b>अपवाद</b> है कि साक्षी तथ्य बताते हैं, राय नहीं।<br>• अधिकार से इनकार करने वाली सरकारी अधिसूचना एक <b>दस्तावेजी तथ्य</b> है जो सुसंगत हो सकती है, परंतु प्रश्न धारा 42 के अंतर्गत सुसंगतता का है, जो रीति-रिवाज पर राय से संबंधित है।<br>• समान प्रावधान <b>विशेषज्ञों की राय (धारा 39) तथा हस्तलेख तुलना</b> पर भी लागू होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि रीति-रिवाज जानने वाले वृद्ध ग्रामीणों की राय सुसंगत है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000071218","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who became the youngest-ever winner of the International Chess Federation (FIDE) Candidates Tournament held in April 2024? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अप्रैल 2024 में आयोजित अंतरराष्ट्रीय शतरंज महासंघ (FIDE) कैंडिडेट्स टूर्नामेंट का सबसे युवा विजेता कौन बना? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R Praggnanandhaa","hi":"आर. प्रग्गनानंद"},"2":{"en":"Vidit Gujrathi","hi":"विदित गुजराती"},"3":{"en":"D Gukesh","hi":"डी. गुकेश"},"4":{"en":"Nihal Sarin","hi":"निहाल सरीन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – D Gukesh</b><br><b>D. Gukesh</b> won the <b>FIDE Candidates Tournament 2024</b> held at Toronto in April 2024 and became the <b>youngest-ever winner</b> of the event, earning the right to challenge the world champion.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Gukesh scored <b>9/14</b> and finished ahead of Hikaru Nakamura, Fabiano Caruana, Ian Nepomniachtchi and R. Praggnanandhaa.<br>• He then defeated <b>Ding Liren</b> in Singapore in December 2024 to become the <b>youngest World Chess Champion</b> at 18.<br>• <b>R. Praggnanandhaa</b> and <b>Vidit Gujrathi</b> also played the 2024 Candidates, and <b>Nihal Sarin</b> is a young Indian GM.<br>• Five Indians took part in the open Candidates 2024, the largest Indian presence in the event.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because D. Gukesh was the youngest winner of the 2024 Candidates Tournament.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – डी. गुकेश</b><br><b>डी. गुकेश (D. Gukesh)</b> ने अप्रैल 2024 में टोरंटो में हुए <b>FIDE कैंडिडेट्स टूर्नामेंट 2024</b> जीता और इस आयोजन के <b>सबसे युवा विजेता</b> बने, जिससे उन्हें विश्व चैंपियन को चुनौती देने का अधिकार मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गुकेश ने <b>9/14</b> अंक प्राप्त किए और हिकारू नाकामुरा, फैबियानो कारुआना, इयान नेपोम्नियाची तथा आर. प्रग्गनानंद से आगे रहे।<br>• उन्होंने दिसंबर 2024 में सिंगापुर में <b>डिंग लिरेन</b> को हराकर 18 वर्ष की आयु में <b>सबसे युवा विश्व शतरंज चैंपियन</b> बनने का कीर्तिमान बनाया।<br>• <b>आर. प्रग्गनानंद</b> तथा <b>विदित गुजराती</b> ने भी 2024 कैंडिडेट्स में भाग लिया, और <b>निहाल सरीन</b> युवा भारतीय ग्रैंडमास्टर हैं।<br>• 2024 के ओपन कैंडिडेट्स में पाँच भारतीयों ने भाग लिया, जो इस आयोजन में भारत की सर्वाधिक भागीदारी थी।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 2024 कैंडिडेट्स टूर्नामेंट के सबसे युवा विजेता डी. गुकेश थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000071219","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who was appointed as the Secretary of the 16<sup>th</sup> Finance Commission of India? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत के 16वें वित्त आयोग के सचिव के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"T.V. Somanathan","hi":"टी. वी. सोमनाथन"},"2":{"en":"Ritvik Ranjanam Pandey","hi":"ऋत्विक रंजनम पांडे"},"3":{"en":"Ajay Seth","hi":"अजय सेठ"},"4":{"en":"Sanjay Malhotra","hi":"संजय मल्होत्रा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Ritvik Ranjanam Pandey</b><br><b>Ritvik Ranjanam Pandey</b>, a senior IAS officer, was appointed <b>Secretary of the 16th Finance Commission of India</b>, which is chaired by <b>Dr Arvind Panagariya</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 16th Finance Commission was constituted in <b>December 2023</b> and covers the award period <b>2026-31</b>.<br>• <b>T.V. Somanathan</b> was the Finance Secretary and later became the Governor of the Reserve Bank of India in December 2024.<br>• <b>Ajay Seth</b> is the Economic Affairs Secretary, and <b>Sanjay Malhotra</b> was Revenue Secretary before becoming RBI Governor.<br>• The Finance Commission is constituted under <b>Article 280</b> every five years to recommend devolution of taxes between the Union and states.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Ritvik Ranjanam Pandey is Secretary of the 16th Finance Commission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ऋत्विक रंजनम पांडे</b><br>वरिष्ठ IAS अधिकारी <b>ऋत्विक रंजनम पांडे (Ritvik Ranjanam Pandey)</b> को <b>भारत के 16वें वित्त आयोग का सचिव</b> नियुक्त किया गया, जिसके अध्यक्ष <b>डॉ. अरविंद पनगढ़िया</b> हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 16वाँ वित्त आयोग <b>दिसंबर 2023</b> में गठित हुआ और इसकी संस्तुति अवधि <b>2026-31</b> है।<br>• <b>टी. वी. सोमनाथन</b> वित्त सचिव थे और दिसंबर 2024 में भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक के गवर्नर बने।<br>• <b>अजय सेठ</b> आर्थिक मामलों के सचिव हैं, और <b>संजय मल्होत्रा</b> राजस्व सचिव रहकर बाद में RBI गवर्नर बने।<br>• वित्त आयोग का गठन <b>अनुच्छेद 280</b> के अंतर्गत प्रत्येक पाँच वर्ष में संघ तथा राज्यों के बीच करों के हस्तांतरण की सिफारिश हेतु होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि ऋत्विक रंजनम पांडे 16वें वित्त आयोग के सचिव हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000071220","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following sportsperson became the first Indian fencer to qualify for the Olympics at the Tokyo 2020 Games (held in 2021)? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी खिलाड़ी टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक (2021 में आयोजित) हेतु अर्हता प्राप्त करने वाली प्रथम भारतीय तलवारबाज बनी? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bhavani Devi","hi":"भवानी देवी"},"2":{"en":"Deepika Kumari","hi":"दीपिका कुमारी"},"3":{"en":"Apurvi Chandela","hi":"अपूर्वी चंदेला"},"4":{"en":"Manu Bhaker","hi":"मनु भाकर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bhavani Devi</b><br><b>Bhavani Devi (C.A. Bhavani Devi)</b> became the <b>first Indian fencer to qualify for the Olympic Games</b>, competing in the women's sabre event at the <b>Tokyo 2020 Olympics</b> held in 2021.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She won her first-round bout against Nadia Ben Azizi of Tunisia before losing in the round of 32.<br>• Bhavani Devi is the first Indian fencer to win a <b>gold at the Commonwealth Fencing Championship</b> and received the Arjuna Award.<br>• She trained in Italy and won medals at the Asian Fencing Championships and the Tournoi Satellite events.<br>• <b>Deepika Kumari</b> is an archer, <b>Apurvi Chandela</b> a shooter and <b>Manu Bhaker</b> a pistol shooter who won two bronze medals at Paris 2024.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because Bhavani Devi was the first Indian fencer to qualify for the Olympics.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भवानी देवी</b><br><b>भवानी देवी (C.A. Bhavani Devi)</b> <b>ओलंपिक खेलों हेतु अर्हता प्राप्त करने वाली प्रथम भारतीय तलवारबाज</b> बनीं और उन्होंने 2021 में आयोजित <b>टोक्यो 2020 ओलंपिक</b> में महिला सैबर स्पर्धा में भाग लिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने पहले दौर में ट्यूनीशिया की नादिया बेन अजीज़ी को हराया और 32 के दौर में बाहर हुईं।<br>• भवानी देवी <b>राष्ट्रमंडल तलवारबाजी चैंपियनशिप में स्वर्ण</b> जीतने वाली प्रथम भारतीय तलवारबाज हैं और उन्हें अर्जुन पुरस्कार मिला।<br>• उन्होंने इटली में प्रशिक्षण लिया तथा एशियाई तलवारबाजी चैंपियनशिप एवं टूर्नोई सैटेलाइट स्पर्धाओं में पदक जीते।<br>• <b>दीपिका कुमारी</b> तीरंदाज हैं, <b>अपूर्वी चंदेला</b> निशानेबाज हैं तथा <b>मनु भाकर</b> पिस्टल निशानेबाज हैं जिन्होंने पेरिस 2024 में दो कांस्य पदक जीते।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि भवानी देवी ओलंपिक हेतु अर्हता प्राप्त करने वाली प्रथम भारतीय तलवारबाज थीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000071221","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"As part of the 1991 economic reforms, the Narasimham Committee recommended a four-tier structure for which sector? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के अंग के रूप में नरसिंहम समिति ने किस क्षेत्र के लिए चार-स्तरीय संरचना की सिफारिश की? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Insurance sector","hi":"बीमा क्षेत्र"},"2":{"en":"Banking sector","hi":"बैंकिंग क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"Energy sector","hi":"ऊर्जा क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"Telecom sector","hi":"दूरसंचार क्षेत्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Banking sector</b><br>The <b>Narasimham Committee (1991)</b> on the financial system recommended a <b>four-tier banking structure</b> – three or four large international banks, eight to ten national banks, local rural banks and rural cooperative banks.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The committee recommended <b>prudential norms, capital adequacy, income recognition and provisioning</b>, and reduction of the SLR and CRR.<br>• It suggested the setting up of <b>Asset Reconstruction Funds and Debt Recovery Tribunals</b>, and allowed entry of private and foreign banks.<br>• The <b>Narasimham Committee II (1998)</b> advised further reforms such as merger of strong banks and a narrow banking concept for weak banks.<br>• Insurance, energy and telecom reforms were handled by other committees such as the Malhotra Committee (insurance) and the TRAI framework (telecom).<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Narasimham Committee recommended a four-tier structure for banking.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बैंकिंग क्षेत्र</b><br>वित्तीय प्रणाली पर <b>नरसिंहम समिति (1991)</b> ने <b>चार-स्तरीय बैंकिंग संरचना</b> की सिफारिश की – तीन या चार बड़े अंतरराष्ट्रीय बैंक, आठ से दस राष्ट्रीय बैंक, स्थानीय ग्रामीण बैंक तथा ग्रामीण सहकारी बैंक।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समिति ने <b>विवेकपूर्ण मानक, पूँजी पर्याप्तता, आय की पहचान तथा प्रावधान</b> और SLR एवं CRR में कमी की सिफारिश की।<br>• इसने <b>परिसंपत्ति पुनर्निर्माण कोष तथा ऋण वसूली अधिकरण</b> बनाने का सुझाव दिया और निजी एवं विदेशी बैंकों के प्रवेश की अनुमति दी।<br>• <b>नरसिंहम समिति II (1998)</b> ने मजबूत बैंकों के विलय तथा दुर्बल बैंकों हेतु संकीर्ण बैंकिंग जैसे आगामी सुधारों की सलाह दी।<br>• बीमा, ऊर्जा तथा दूरसंचार सुधार अन्य समितियों द्वारा देखे गए, जैसे मल्होत्रा समिति (बीमा) तथा TRAI रूपरेखा (दूरसंचार)।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि नरसिंहम समिति ने बैंकिंग के लिए चार-स्तरीय संरचना की सिफारिश की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000071222","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"At which venue was the second Test of India's tour of England during the 2025-27 International Cricket Council (ICC) World Test Championship cycle played from 2-6 July 2025? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"2025-27 अंतरराष्ट्रीय क्रिकेट परिषद (ICC) विश्व टेस्ट चैंपियनशिप चक्र में इंग्लैंड दौरे का दूसरा टेस्ट 2-6 जुलाई 2025 तक किस स्थान पर खेला गया? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord's, London","hi":"लॉर्ड्स, लंदन"},"2":{"en":"Old Trafford, Manchester","hi":"ओल्ड ट्रैफर्ड, मैनचेस्टर"},"3":{"en":"Edgbaston, Birmingham","hi":"एजबेस्टन, बर्मिंघम"},"4":{"en":"Headingley, Leeds","hi":"हेडिंग्ले, लीड्स"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Edgbaston, Birmingham</b><br>The <b>second Test</b> of India's tour of England in the <b>2025-27 ICC World Test Championship</b> cycle was played at <b>Edgbaston, Birmingham</b>, from <b>2 to 6 July 2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The five-Test series began at <b>Headingley, Leeds</b> (first Test) and continued at Edgbaston, Lord's and Old Trafford, ending at The Oval.<br>• India won the series <b>2-1</b>, with two matches drawn, under the captaincy of Shubman Gill.<br>• The <b>World Test Championship</b> was launched in 2019 and its final is played at The Oval, London.<br>• India had reached the WTC finals in 2021, 2023 and 2025, losing to Australia in 2023.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the second Test of the 2025 England tour was played at Edgbaston.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – एजबेस्टन, बर्मिंघम</b><br><b>2025-27 ICC विश्व टेस्ट चैंपियनशिप</b> चक्र में इंग्लैंड दौरे का <b>दूसरा टेस्ट</b> <b>2 से 6 जुलाई 2025</b> तक <b>एजबेस्टन, बर्मिंघम</b> में खेला गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पाँच टेस्ट की श्रृंखला <b>हेडिंग्ले, लीड्स</b> (प्रथम टेस्ट) से आरंभ हुई और एजबेस्टन, लॉर्ड्स तथा ओल्ड ट्रैफर्ड में चलकर द ओवल में समाप्त हुई।<br>• शुभमन गिल की कप्तानी में भारत ने दो मैच ड्रॉ रहते हुए श्रृंखला <b>2-1</b> से जीती।<br>• <b>विश्व टेस्ट चैंपियनशिप</b> 2019 में शुरू हुई और इसका फाइनल लंदन के द ओवल में होता है।<br>• भारत 2021, 2023 तथा 2025 में WTC फाइनल में पहुँचा और 2023 में ऑस्ट्रेलिया से हारा।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 2025 के इंग्लैंड दौरे का दूसरा टेस्ट एजबेस्टन में खेला गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000071223","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which city was the 2025 Men's Hockey Asia Cup held from 29 August to 7 September 2025, where India won its fourth title and secured direct qualification for the 2026 Federation Internationale de Hockey (FIH) Hockey World Cup? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"29 अगस्त से 7 सितंबर 2025 तक आयोजित पुरुष हॉकी एशिया कप 2025 किस नगर में हुआ, जहाँ भारत ने अपना चौथा खिताब जीता तथा 2026 FIH हॉकी विश्व कप हेतु सीधी अर्हता प्राप्त की? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kalinga Stadium, Bhubaneswar","hi":"कलिंगा स्टेडियम, भुवनेश्वर"},"2":{"en":"Major Dhyan Chand Stadium, New Delhi","hi":"मेजर ध्यानचंद स्टेडियम, नई दिल्ली"},"3":{"en":"Bihar Sports University Hockey Stadium, Rajgir","hi":"बिहार स्पोर्ट्स यूनिवर्सिटी हॉकी स्टेडियम, राजगीर"},"4":{"en":"Birsa Munda Hockey Stadium, Rourkela","hi":"बिरसा मुंडा हॉकी स्टेडियम, राउरकेला"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Bihar Sports University Hockey Stadium, Rajgir</b><br>The <b>2025 Men's Hockey Asia Cup</b> was held from <b>29 August to 7 September 2025</b> at the <b>Bihar Sports University Hockey Stadium in Rajgir, Bihar</b>, where India beat South Korea in the final to win its <b>fourth Asia Cup title</b> and qualify directly for the <b>2026 FIH Hockey World Cup</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India had earlier won the Asia Cup in <b>2003, 2007 and 2017</b>, and this was the first time the tournament was held at Rajgir.<br>• The win secured India's place in the 2026 World Cup to be co-hosted by <b>Belgium and the Netherlands</b>.<br>• The <b>Kalinga Stadium, Bhubaneswar</b> and <b>Birsa Munda Hockey Stadium, Rourkela</b> hosted the 2023 Men's World Cup, and the Major Dhyan Chand Stadium is in Delhi.<br>• The Asia Cup is organised by the <b>Asian Hockey Federation</b>, and India is the most successful team in the competition.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the 2025 Men's Hockey Asia Cup was held at Rajgir.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बिहार स्पोर्ट्स यूनिवर्सिटी हॉकी स्टेडियम, राजगीर</b><br><b>पुरुष हॉकी एशिया कप 2025</b> <b>29 अगस्त से 7 सितंबर 2025</b> तक बिहार के <b>राजगीर स्थित बिहार स्पोर्ट्स यूनिवर्सिटी हॉकी स्टेडियम</b> में हुआ, जहाँ भारत ने फाइनल में दक्षिण कोरिया को हराकर अपना <b>चौथा एशिया कप खिताब</b> जीता और <b>2026 FIH हॉकी विश्व कप</b> हेतु सीधी अर्हता प्राप्त की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत ने इससे पहले <b>2003, 2007 तथा 2017</b> में एशिया कप जीता था, और यह पहली बार था जब यह टूर्नामेंट राजगीर में हुआ।<br>• इस जीत से भारत को <b>बेल्जियम तथा नीदरलैंड</b> की सह-मेजबानी वाले 2026 विश्व कप में स्थान मिला।<br>• <b>कलिंगा स्टेडियम, भुवनेश्वर</b> तथा <b>बिरसा मुंडा हॉकी स्टेडियम, राउरकेला</b> ने 2023 पुरुष विश्व कप की मेजबानी की थी, और मेजर ध्यानचंद स्टेडियम दिल्ली में है।<br>• एशिया कप <b>एशियाई हॉकी महासंघ</b> आयोजित करता है, और भारत इस प्रतियोगिता की सबसे सफल टीम है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि पुरुष हॉकी एशिया कप 2025 राजगीर में हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000071224","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"A deep-focus earthquake occurs at a depth of 600 km. A seismic station detects strong P-waves but no S-waves after they pass through Earth’s outer core. What does this observation suggest about the nature of Earth’s outer core? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"600 किमी की गहराई पर एक गहन-केंद्रित भूकंप होता है। एक भूकंपीय केंद्र पृथ्वी के बाहरी क्रोड से गुज़रने के बाद तीव्र P-तरंगें दर्ज करता है, परंतु S-तरंगें नहीं। यह अवलोकन पृथ्वी के बाहरी क्रोड की प्रकृति के बारे में क्या संकेत देता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Outer core is solid iron","hi":"बाहरी क्रोड ठोस लोहा है"},"2":{"en":"Outer core is liquid","hi":"बाहरी क्रोड तरल है"},"3":{"en":"Mantle is liquid","hi":"मैंटल तरल है"},"4":{"en":"Inner core is gaseous","hi":"आंतरिक क्रोड गैसीय है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Outer core is liquid</b><br>The absence of <b>S-waves</b> beyond the outer core shows that the <b>outer core is liquid</b>, because S-waves are <b>transverse waves that cannot travel through liquids</b>, while P-waves (longitudinal) can pass through them.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The boundary where S-waves disappear is the <b>Gutenberg discontinuity</b> at a depth of about 2,900 km.<br>• The outer core is made mainly of <b>liquid iron and nickel</b>, and its motion generates the earth's magnetic field through the dynamo effect.<br>• The <b>inner core is solid</b> because of very high pressure, and P-waves speed up again on entering it.<br>• The mantle is <b>solid but plastic</b> and transmits both P and S waves, so options (1), (3) and (4) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the absence of S-waves indicates a liquid outer core.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बाहरी क्रोड तरल है</b><br>बाहरी क्रोड के आगे <b>S-तरंगों</b> की अनुपस्थिति दर्शाती है कि <b>बाहरी क्रोड तरल</b> है, क्योंकि S-तरंगें <b>अनुप्रस्थ तरंगें हैं जो तरल में नहीं चल सकतीं</b>, जबकि P-तरंगें (अनुदैर्घ्य) उनमें से गुज़र सकती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• जहाँ S-तरंगें लुप्त होती हैं वह सीमा लगभग 2,900 किमी गहराई पर <b>गुटेनबर्ग असंबद्धता</b> है।<br>• बाहरी क्रोड मुख्यतः <b>तरल लोहा तथा निकल</b> से बना है, और उसकी गति डायनेमो प्रभाव से पृथ्वी का चुंबकीय क्षेत्र बनाती है।<br>• अत्यधिक दाब के कारण <b>आंतरिक क्रोड ठोस</b> है, और उसमें प्रवेश करते ही P-तरंगों की चाल पुनः बढ़ जाती है।<br>• मैंटल <b>ठोस परंतु सुघट्य</b> है और P तथा S दोनों तरंगें संचारित करता है, इसलिए विकल्प (1), (3) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि S-तरंगों का अभाव तरल बाहरी क्रोड दर्शाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000071225","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"Natural capital is often compared to money deposited in a bank. Which of the following best explains the implication of this analogy? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"प्राकृतिक पूँजी की तुलना प्रायः बैंक में जमा धन से की जाती है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा इस उपमा के निहितार्थ का सर्वोत्तम वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Natural resources can always regenerate if managed by governments.","hi":"यदि सरकारें प्रबंधन करें तो प्राकृतिक संसाधन सदैव पुनः उत्पन्न हो सकते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Sustainable use means utilizing only the regenerative capacity of resources.","hi":"सतत उपयोग का अर्थ है संसाधनों की केवल पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता का उपयोग करना।"},"3":{"en":"Non-renewable resources are equivalent to fixed deposits.","hi":"अक्षय संसाधन सावधि जमा के समान हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Economic growth depends entirely on resource extraction.","hi":"आर्थिक वृद्धि पूर्णतः संसाधन निष्कर्षण पर निर्भर है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sustainable use means utilizing only the regenerative capacity of resources.</b><br>The bank-deposit analogy for <b>natural capital</b> means that we may use only the <b>'interest' – the regenerative capacity</b> of natural resources – and must not consume the <b>'capital' or stock</b>, so that future generations inherit an intact resource base.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• This is the idea behind <b>sustainable development</b> and the <b>Hartwick rule</b>, which requires reinvesting resource rents in other capital.<br>• For <b>renewable resources</b> the harvest rate should not exceed the regeneration rate; for non-renewable resources, depletion must be offset by investment.<br>• The analogy does not claim that all resources regenerate, that non-renewables equal fixed deposits, or that growth depends entirely on extraction, so options (1), (3) and (4) are wrong.<br>• 'Natural capital' includes forests, soil, water, fisheries and the atmosphere, and is measured in the <b>System of Environmental-Economic Accounting</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because sustainable use means living on the regenerative capacity of resources.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सतत उपयोग का अर्थ है संसाधनों की केवल पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता का उपयोग करना।</b><br><b>प्राकृतिक पूँजी</b> की बैंक-जमा उपमा का अर्थ है कि हम केवल <b>'ब्याज' – अर्थात प्राकृतिक संसाधनों की पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता</b> – का उपयोग कर सकते हैं और <b>'मूलधन' या भंडार</b> को नहीं गँवा सकते, जिससे भावी पीढ़ियों को अक्षुण्ण संसाधन आधार मिले।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यही विचार <b>सतत विकास</b> तथा <b>हार्टविक नियम</b> का आधार है, जो संसाधन लगान की पुनर्निवेश की अपेक्षा करता है।<br>• <b>नवीकरणीय संसाधनों</b> में उपज दर पुनरुत्पादन दर से अधिक नहीं होनी चाहिए; अक्षय संसाधनों में कमी की पूर्ति निवेश से होनी चाहिए।<br>• यह उपमा यह नहीं कहती कि सभी संसाधन पुनः बनते हैं, न यह कि अक्षय संसाधन सावधि जमा के समान हैं, और न यह कि वृद्धि पूर्णतः निष्कर्षण पर निर्भर है, इसलिए विकल्प (1), (3) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br>• 'प्राकृतिक पूँजी' में वन, मृदा, जल, मत्स्य तथा वायुमंडल सम्मिलित हैं और इसे <b>पर्यावरण-आर्थिक लेखांकन प्रणाली</b> में मापा जाता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि सतत उपयोग संसाधनों की पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता पर जीवन-यापन है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000071226","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"If a consumer’s income increases, resulting in greater consumption of good X and lower consumption of good Y, which of the following is correct? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि उपभोक्ता की आय बढ़ने से वस्तु X की खपत अधिक तथा वस्तु Y की खपत कम हो जाती है, तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा सही है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both X and Y are inferior goods.","hi":"X तथा Y दोनों घटिया वस्तुएँ हैं।"},"2":{"en":"X is an inferior good, while Y is a normal good.","hi":"X घटिया वस्तु है, जबकि Y सामान्य वस्तु है।"},"3":{"en":"X is a normal good, while Y is an inferior good.","hi":"X सामान्य वस्तु है, जबकि Y घटिया वस्तु है।"},"4":{"en":"Both X and Y are normal goods.","hi":"X तथा Y दोनों सामान्य वस्तुएँ हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – X is a normal good, while Y is an inferior good.</b><br>When income rises, demand for a <b>normal good increases</b> and demand for an <b>inferior good decreases</b>, so <b>X is a normal good</b> and <b>Y is an inferior good</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Income elasticity of demand is <b>positive for normal goods</b> and <b>negative for inferior goods</b>; for necessities it is positive but less than one, and for luxuries more than one.<br>• Examples of inferior goods are coarse cereals, cheap clothing and local transport, which are replaced by better substitutes as income rises.<br>• A <b>Giffen good</b> is a special inferior good whose demand falls when price falls, violating the law of demand.<br>• If both goods were normal, consumption of both would rise, so options (1) and (4) are wrong, and option (2) reverses the relationship.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because X is normal and Y is inferior.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – X सामान्य वस्तु है, जबकि Y घटिया वस्तु है।</b><br>आय बढ़ने पर <b>सामान्य वस्तु</b> की माँग <b>बढ़ती</b> है तथा <b>घटिया वस्तु</b> की माँग <b>घटती</b> है, इसलिए <b>X सामान्य वस्तु</b> तथा <b>Y घटिया वस्तु</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• माँग की आय लोच <b>सामान्य वस्तुओं के लिए धनात्मक</b> तथा <b>घटिया वस्तुओं के लिए ऋणात्मक</b> होती है; आवश्यक वस्तुओं में यह एक से कम तथा विलासिता की वस्तुओं में एक से अधिक होती है।<br>• घटिया वस्तुओं के उदाहरण मोटे अनाज, सस्ते वस्त्र तथा स्थानीय परिवहन हैं, जिन्हें आय बढ़ने पर बेहतर विकल्प प्रतिस्थापित कर देते हैं।<br>• <b>गिफेन वस्तु</b> विशेष घटिया वस्तु है जिसकी माँग कीमत घटने पर घटती है, जो माँग के नियम का उल्लंघन है।<br>• यदि दोनों वस्तुएँ सामान्य होतीं तो दोनों की खपत बढ़ती, इसलिए विकल्प (1) तथा (4) गलत हैं, और विकल्प (2) संबंध उलट देता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि X सामान्य तथा Y घटिया वस्तु है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000071227","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Nutrients","question":{"en":"A child develops soft and weak bones that become bowed because of improper mineralisation. Which deficiency disease is most likely responsible for this condition? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अनुचित खनिजीकरण के कारण एक बच्चे की हड्डियाँ मुलायम तथा कमजोर होकर मुड़ जाती हैं। इस स्थिति के लिए सर्वाधिक संभावित कमी-रोग कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Scurvy","hi":"स्कर्वी"},"2":{"en":"Rickets","hi":"रिकेट्स"},"3":{"en":"Beriberi","hi":"बेरीबेरी"},"4":{"en":"Anemia","hi":"एनीमिया"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Rickets</b><br><b>Rickets</b> is caused by a deficiency of <b>vitamin D</b>, calcium or phosphate, which leads to poor mineralisation of bones, making them <b>soft, weak and bowed</b> in growing children.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Vitamin D is synthesised in the skin on exposure to <b>sunlight</b> and helps absorb calcium and phosphorus from the intestine.<br>• In adults the corresponding condition is <b>osteomalacia</b>, and severe deficiency causes tetany from low blood calcium.<br>• <b>Scurvy</b> is caused by deficiency of vitamin C, <b>beriberi</b> by vitamin B1 (thiamine) and <b>anaemia</b> mainly by iron or vitamin B12 deficiency.<br>• Sources of vitamin D include sunlight, fish oil, egg yolk and fortified milk, and 'bow legs' and knock knees are classic signs of rickets.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because soft and bowed bones from poor mineralisation indicate rickets.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रिकेट्स</b><br><b>रिकेट्स</b> <b>विटामिन D</b>, कैल्शियम या फॉस्फेट की कमी से होता है, जिससे हड्डियों का खनिजीकरण ठीक से नहीं होता और बढ़ते बच्चों की हड्डियाँ <b>मुलायम, कमजोर तथा मुड़ी हुई</b> हो जाती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विटामिन D <b>सूर्य के प्रकाश</b> से त्वचा में बनता है और आंत से कैल्शियम तथा फॉस्फोरस के अवशोषण में सहायक है।<br>• वयस्कों में इसी से संबंधित रोग <b>ऑस्टियोमलेशिया</b> है, और गंभीर कमी से रक्त-कैल्शियम घटने पर टिटनी होती है।<br>• <b>स्कर्वी</b> विटामिन C की कमी से, <b>बेरीबेरी</b> विटामिन B1 (थायमिन) की कमी से तथा <b>एनीमिया</b> मुख्यतः लोहा या विटामिन B12 की कमी से होता है।<br>• विटामिन D के स्रोत सूर्य प्रकाश, मछली तेल, अंडे की जर्दी तथा फोर्टिफाइड दूध हैं, और टेढ़े पैर (bow legs) रिकेट्स के प्रमुख लक्षण हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि अनुचित खनिजीकरण से मुलायम एवं मुड़ी हड्डियाँ रिकेट्स दर्शाती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000071228","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Plant and Animal Kingdom","question":{"en":"On a hot day, a plant loses water vapour from its leaves through tiny openings on the leaf surface. What are these openings called? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"गर्म दिन में पौधा पत्तियों की सतह पर छोटे छिद्रों से जलवाष्प खोता है। इन छिद्रों को क्या कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Veins","hi":"शिराएँ"},"2":{"en":"Chloroplasts","hi":"हरितलवक"},"3":{"en":"Root hairs","hi":"मूलरोम"},"4":{"en":"Stomata","hi":"रंध्र"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Stomata</b><br><b>Stomata</b> are tiny openings on the leaf surface, mainly on the lower epidermis, through which a plant loses water vapour by <b>transpiration</b> and exchanges gases during photosynthesis.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Each stoma is guarded by two <b>guard cells</b>; when they swell with water the pore opens, and when they lose water it closes.<br>• Transpiration pull helps in the <b>ascent of sap</b> and cools the plant on a hot day.<br>• <b>Veins</b> carry water and food, <b>chloroplasts</b> are the site of photosynthesis and <b>root hairs</b> absorb water and minerals from the soil.<br>• In xerophytes stomata are sunken or reduced, and in floating leaves such as lotus the stomata are on the upper surface.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the openings that lose water vapour from leaves are stomata.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – रंध्र</b><br><b>रंध्र (Stomata)</b> पत्ती की सतह, मुख्यतः निचली बाह्यत्वचा पर स्थित सूक्ष्म छिद्र हैं, जिनसे पौधा <b>वाष्पोत्सर्जन</b> द्वारा जलवाष्प खोता है तथा प्रकाश संश्लेषण के समय गैसों का विनिमय करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रत्येक रंध्र की रक्षा दो <b>रक्षक कोशिकाएँ</b> करती हैं; जल से फूलने पर छिद्र खुलता है और जल खोने पर बंद हो जाता है।<br>• वाष्पोत्सर्जन कर्षण <b>रसारोहण</b> में सहायक है और गर्म दिन में पौधे को ठंडा रखता है।<br>• <b>शिराएँ</b> जल तथा भोजन पहुँचाती हैं, <b>हरितलवक</b> प्रकाश संश्लेषण का स्थल हैं और <b>मूलरोम</b> मिट्टी से जल एवं खनिज अवशोषित करते हैं।<br>• मरुस्थलीय पौधों (xerophytes) में रंध्र धँसे या कम होते हैं, तथा कमल जैसी तैरती पत्तियों में रंध्र ऊपरी सतह पर होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि पत्तियों से जलवाष्प खोने वाले छिद्र रंध्र हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000071229","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"Under the Dyarchy system introduced by the Government of India Act 1919, provincial subjects were divided into 'Reserved' subjects and which other category? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत सरकार अधिनियम 1919 द्वारा लागू द्वैध शासन प्रणाली के अंतर्गत प्रांतीय विषय 'आरक्षित' विषयों तथा किस अन्य श्रेणी में विभाजित किए गए थे? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Federal subjects","hi":"संघीय विषय"},"2":{"en":"Transferred subjects","hi":"हस्तांतरित विषय"},"3":{"en":"Concurrent subjects","hi":"समवर्ती विषय"},"4":{"en":"Residuary subjects","hi":"अवशिष्ट विषय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Transferred subjects</b><br>The <b>Government of India Act, 1919</b> introduced <b>dyarchy</b> in the provinces, dividing provincial subjects into <b>'Reserved' subjects</b>, administered by the Governor with his executive council, and <b>'Transferred' subjects</b>, administered by ministers responsible to the provincial legislature.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Reserved subjects included <b>police, justice, finance and land revenue</b>, while transferred subjects included <b>education, health, local self-government and agriculture</b>.<br>• The Act introduced <b>bicameralism</b> and direct elections in the provinces and created the office of the <b>High Commissioner for India</b>.<br>• It provided for the <b>Public Service Commission</b> and the separation of central and provincial budgets.<br>• Dyarchy failed because of the <b>rigid division of subjects and the Governor's overriding powers</b>, and was abolished by the Government of India Act, 1935, which introduced provincial autonomy.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because provincial subjects were divided into reserved and transferred subjects.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – हस्तांतरित विषय</b><br><b>भारत सरकार अधिनियम, 1919</b> ने प्रांतों में <b>द्वैध शासन</b> लागू किया और प्रांतीय विषयों को <b>'आरक्षित' विषयों</b> में, जिन्हें गवर्नर अपनी कार्यकारी परिषद के साथ संभालता था, तथा <b>'हस्तांतरित' विषयों</b> में विभाजित किया, जिन्हें प्रांतीय विधानमंडल के प्रति उत्तरदायी मंत्री संभालते थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• आरक्षित विषयों में <b>पुलिस, न्याय, वित्त तथा भू-राजस्व</b> थे, जबकि हस्तांतरित विषयों में <b>शिक्षा, स्वास्थ्य, स्थानीय स्वशासन तथा कृषि</b> थे।<br>• इस अधिनियम ने प्रांतों में <b>द्विसदनीय व्यवस्था</b> तथा प्रत्यक्ष चुनाव शुरू किए और <b>भारत के उच्चायुक्त</b> का पद बनाया।<br>• इसमें <b>लोक सेवा आयोग</b> तथा केंद्रीय एवं प्रांतीय बजटों के पृथक्करण का प्रावधान था।<br>• विषयों के कठोर विभाजन तथा गवर्नर की अधिक्रमण शक्तियों के कारण द्वैध शासन विफल रहा और इसे भारत सरकार अधिनियम, 1935 ने समाप्त कर प्रांतीय स्वायत्तता लागू की।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि प्रांतीय विषय आरक्षित तथा हस्तांतरित विषयों में विभाजित थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000071230","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946, while rejecting an outright separate state of Pakistan, instead proposed which alternative constitutional arrangement? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1946 की कैबिनेट मिशन योजना ने पाकिस्तान के पूर्णतः पृथक राज्य को अस्वीकार करते हुए इसके विकल्प के रूप में कौन-सी संवैधानिक व्यवस्था प्रस्तावित की? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A loose three-tier federal structure with grouped provinces","hi":"समूहित प्रांतों वाली शिथिल त्रि-स्तरीय संघीय संरचना"},"2":{"en":"Complete Dominion status without any partition","hi":"बिना किसी विभाजन के पूर्ण डोमिनियन स्थिति"},"3":{"en":"Continuation of separate electorates indefinitely","hi":"पृथक निर्वाचन मंडलों की अनिश्चितकालीन निरंतरता"},"4":{"en":"A unitary state with no provincial powers at all","hi":"प्रांतीय शक्तियों के बिना पूर्णतः एकात्मक राज्य"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – A loose three-tier federal structure with grouped provinces</b><br>The <b>Cabinet Mission Plan of 1946</b> rejected a separate sovereign Pakistan and instead proposed a <b>loose three-tier federal structure</b> – a Union of India at the top with only foreign affairs, defence and communications, <b>groups of provinces (Sections A, B and C)</b> in the middle, and the provinces at the bottom.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Mission comprised <b>Pethick-Lawrence, Stafford Cripps and A.V. Alexander</b>, who arrived in India in March 1946.<br>• It proposed a <b>Constituent Assembly</b> elected by the provincial assemblies, with seats allotted to the three communities, and an interim government.<br>• Section A covered the predominantly Hindu provinces, <b>Section B the Muslim-majority provinces of the north-west</b> and <b>Section C Bengal and Assam</b>.<br>• The plan was accepted by the Congress and the Muslim League initially, but the League withdrew its acceptance and observed 'Direct Action Day' in August 1946.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the Mission proposed a loose three-tier federal structure with grouped provinces.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – समूहित प्रांतों वाली शिथिल त्रि-स्तरीय संघीय संरचना</b><br><b>1946 की कैबिनेट मिशन योजना</b> ने पृथक संप्रभु पाकिस्तान को अस्वीकार किया और इसके स्थान पर <b>शिथिल त्रि-स्तरीय संघीय संरचना</b> प्रस्तावित की – शीर्ष पर <b>भारत संघ</b>, जिसके पास केवल विदेश, रक्षा तथा संचार हों; मध्य में <b>प्रांतों के समूह (खंड A, B तथा C)</b>; और तल पर प्रांत।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मिशन में <b>पेथिक-लॉरेंस, स्टैफर्ड क्रिप्स तथा ए. वी. अलेक्जेंडर</b> सम्मिलित थे, जो मार्च 1946 में भारत आए।<br>• इसने प्रांतीय विधानमंडलों द्वारा निर्वाचित <b>संविधान सभा</b> का प्रस्ताव किया, जिसमें तीन समुदायों को स्थान आवंटित थे, साथ ही अंतरिम सरकार का भी।<br>• खंड A में हिंदू-बहुल प्रांत, <b>खंड B में उत्तर-पश्चिम के मुस्लिम-बहुल प्रांत</b> तथा <b>खंड C में बंगाल एवं असम</b> थे।<br>• योजना को कांग्रेस तथा मुस्लिम लीग ने प्रारंभ में स्वीकार किया, परंतु लीग ने स्वीकृति वापस लेकर अगस्त 1946 में 'प्रत्यक्ष कार्रवाई दिवस' मनाया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि मिशन ने समूहित प्रांतों वाली शिथिल त्रि-स्तरीय संघीय संरचना प्रस्तावित की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000071231","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the expression: \\(\\frac{(0.2 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.2 + 0.04 \\times 0.04 \\times 0.04)}{(0.4 \\times 0.4 \\times 0.4 + 0.08 \\times 0.08 \\times 0.08)}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"व्यंजक को सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{(0.2 \\times 0.2 \\times 0.2 + 0.04 \\times 0.04 \\times 0.04)}{(0.4 \\times 0.4 \\times 0.4 + 0.08 \\times 0.08 \\times 0.08)}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Numerator \\(= 0.008 + 0.000064 = 0.008064\\)<br>Denominator \\(= 0.064 + 0.000512 = 0.064512\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{0.008064}{0.064512}\\)<br>Since \\(0.064512 = 8 \\times 0.008064\\), the value is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\).</b>","hi":"अंश \\(= 0.008 + 0.000064 = 0.008064\\)<br>हर \\(= 0.064 + 0.000512 = 0.064512\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{0.008064}{0.064512}\\)<br>चूँकि \\(0.064512 = 8 \\times 0.008064\\), मान \\(\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000071232","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"If the graph of the line y = mx + 4 passes through the point (2, 10), what is the value of m? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि रेखा y = mx + 4 का ग्राफ बिंदु (2, 10) से गुज़रता है, तो m का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Substitute \\(x = 2\\), \\(y = 10\\):<br>\\(10 = 2m + 4 \\Rightarrow 2m = 6\\)<br>\\(m = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"\\(x = 2\\), \\(y = 10\\) रखिए:<br>\\(10 = 2m + 4 \\Rightarrow 2m = 6\\)<br>\\(m = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000071233","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"If the lines ax + 2y = 10 and 3x + ay = 15 are parallel but not coincident, what is the value of a? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि रेखाएँ ax + 2y = 10 और 3x + ay = 15 समांतर हैं परंतु संपाती नहीं हैं, तो a का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(a = \\sqrt{6}, a = -\\sqrt{6}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(a = \\sqrt{3}, a = -\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(a = \\sqrt{2}, a = -\\sqrt{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(a = \\sqrt{5}, a = -\\sqrt{5}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For parallel lines, \\(\\frac{a_1}{a_2} = \\frac{b_1}{b_2}\\):<br>\\(\\frac{a}{3} = \\frac{2}{a} \\Rightarrow a^2 = 6 \\Rightarrow a = \\pm\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>These values do not make the lines coincident (the constant ratio differs), so \\(\\boxed{a = \\sqrt{6},\\ a = -\\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(a = \\sqrt{6}, a = -\\sqrt{6}\\).</b>","hi":"समांतर रेखाओं के लिए, \\(\\frac{a_1}{a_2} = \\frac{b_1}{b_2}\\):<br>\\(\\frac{a}{3} = \\frac{2}{a} \\Rightarrow a^2 = 6 \\Rightarrow a = \\pm\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>इन मानों से रेखाएँ संपाती नहीं होतीं (अचर का अनुपात भिन्न है), अतः \\(\\boxed{a = \\sqrt{6},\\ a = -\\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(a = \\sqrt{6}, a = -\\sqrt{6}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000071234","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"From a point exactly midway between two towers P and Q, the angles of elevation of their tops are 30° and 45° respectively. Find the ratio of the height of P to that of Q. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो मीनारों P और Q के ठीक बीच में स्थित एक बिंदु से उनके शिखरों के उन्नयन कोण क्रमशः 30° और 45° हैं। P की ऊँचाई का Q की ऊँचाई से अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"√3 : 1"},"2":{"en":"√3 : 2"},"3":{"en":"1 : √3"},"4":{"en":"2 : √3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the midpoint be at distance \\(d\\) from each tower.<br>Height of P \\(= d\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{d}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>Height of Q \\(= d\\tan 45^\\circ = d\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{d/\\sqrt{3}}{d} = 1 : \\sqrt{3}\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{1 : \\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1 : √3.</b>","hi":"मध्य बिंदु प्रत्येक मीनार से \\(d\\) दूरी पर मानिए।<br>P की ऊँचाई \\(= d\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{d}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>Q की ऊँचाई \\(= d\\tan 45^\\circ = d\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{d/\\sqrt{3}}{d} = 1 : \\sqrt{3}\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{1 : \\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1 : √3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000071235","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If the volume of a cube is reduced to 21.6%, find the percentage decrease in the side. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि एक घन का आयतन 21.6% तक घटा दिया जाए, तो भुजा में प्रतिशत कमी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25%"},"2":{"en":"40%"},"3":{"en":"32%"},"4":{"en":"51%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{V'}{V} = 0.216 = (0.6)^3\\)<br>So the new side is \\(0.6a\\), a decrease of \\(0.4a\\)<br>Percentage decrease = \\(40\\%\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{40\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 40%.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{V'}{V} = 0.216 = (0.6)^3\\)<br>अतः नई भुजा \\(0.6a\\) है, अर्थात् \\(0.4a\\) की कमी<br>प्रतिशत कमी = \\(40\\%\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{40\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 40% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000071236","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: \\(\\frac{\\tan A+\\cot A}{\\sec A \\cdot \\csc A}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\tan A+\\cot A}{\\sec A \\cdot \\csc A}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = \\frac{\\sin A}{\\cos A} + \\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\frac{\\sin^2A + \\cos^2A}{\\sin A\\cos A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A}\\)<br>\\(\\sec A \\cdot \\csc A = \\frac{1}{\\cos A} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sin A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A}\\)<br>Expression \\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = \\frac{\\sin A}{\\cos A} + \\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\frac{\\sin^2A + \\cos^2A}{\\sin A\\cos A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A}\\)<br>\\(\\sec A \\cdot \\csc A = \\frac{1}{\\cos A} \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sin A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A}\\)<br>व्यंजक \\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000071237","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A parallelogram has adjacent sides of length 15 cm and 9 cm. If the distance between the longer sides is 6 cm, what is the distance between the shorter sides? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समांतर चतुर्भुज की आसन्न भुजाएँ 15 cm और 9 cm हैं। यदि लंबी भुजाओं के बीच की दूरी 6 cm है, तो छोटी भुजाओं के बीच की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10 cm"},"2":{"en":"8 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"9 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Area = base × corresponding height<br>\\(= 15 \\times 6 = 90\\) cm²<br>For the shorter side: \\(9 \\times h = 90 \\Rightarrow h = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"क्षेत्रफल = आधार × संगत ऊँचाई<br>\\(= 15 \\times 6 = 90\\) cm²<br>छोटी भुजा के लिए: \\(9 \\times h = 90 \\Rightarrow h = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000071238","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(k \\cdot \\tan 45^\\circ \\cdot \\sin 60^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sec^2 45^\\circ \\cdot \\cot 30^\\circ}{\\csc 60^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 60^\\circ}\\), then find the value of k. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(k \\cdot \\tan 45^\\circ \\cdot \\sin 60^\\circ \\cdot \\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sec^2 45^\\circ \\cdot \\cot 30^\\circ}{\\csc 60^\\circ \\cdot \\tan 60^\\circ}\\) है, तो k का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{7}}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{6}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"LHS = \\(k \\times 1 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{3k}{4}\\)<br>RHS = \\(\\frac{2 \\times \\sqrt{3}}{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3k}{4} = \\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow k = \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}\\).</b>","hi":"बायाँ पक्ष = \\(k \\times 1 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\frac{3k}{4}\\)<br>दायाँ पक्ष = \\(\\frac{2 \\times \\sqrt{3}}{\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\times \\sqrt{3}} = \\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2} = \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3k}{4} = \\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow k = \\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000071239","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\left(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1+\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta}\\right)\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(\\left(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1+\\sin\\theta} + \\frac{1+\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\tan\\theta+\\cot\\theta}\\right)\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2\\sin\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\tan\\theta\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(2\\cos\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"First bracket \\(= \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta + (1 + \\sin\\theta)^2}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta + 1 + 2\\sin\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2(1 + \\sin\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>Also \\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\), so the second bracket is \\(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\)<br>Expression \\(= \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} \\times \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{2\\sin\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(2\\sin\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"पहला कोष्ठक \\(= \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta + (1 + \\sin\\theta)^2}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta + 1 + 2\\sin\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2(1 + \\sin\\theta)}{\\cos\\theta(1 + \\sin\\theta)} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta}\\)<br>साथ ही \\(\\tan\\theta + \\cot\\theta = \\frac{1}{\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta}\\), अतः दूसरा कोष्ठक \\(\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\) है<br>व्यंजक \\(= \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} \\times \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta = \\boxed{2\\sin\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(2\\sin\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000071240","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism stands on a square base of side a. If the height of the prism is doubled and the side of the square base is halved, what is the ratio of the new volume to the original volume? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समकोणीय प्रिज्म भुजा a वाले वर्गाकार आधार पर खड़ा है। यदि प्रिज्म की ऊँचाई दोगुनी कर दी जाए और वर्गाकार आधार की भुजा आधी कर दी जाए, तो नए आयतन का मूल आयतन से अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1:2"},"2":{"en":"1:3"},"3":{"en":"1:4"},"4":{"en":"1:1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Original volume \\(= a^2 h\\)<br>New volume \\(= \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2(2h) = \\frac{a^2h}{2}\\)<br>Ratio = \\(\\frac{a^2h/2}{a^2h} = 1 : 2\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{1:2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1:2.</b>","hi":"मूल आयतन \\(= a^2 h\\)<br>नया आयतन \\(= \\left(\\frac{a}{2}\\right)^2(2h) = \\frac{a^2h}{2}\\)<br>अनुपात = \\(\\frac{a^2h/2}{a^2h} = 1 : 2\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{1:2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1:2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000071241","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A mixture of acid and water contains 20 percent acid. When 10 liters of water is added to the mixture, then the percentage of acid becomes 15 percent. What is the original quantity of mixture? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अम्ल और जल के मिश्रण में 20 प्रतिशत अम्ल है। जब मिश्रण में 10 लीटर जल मिलाया जाता है, तो अम्ल का प्रतिशत 15 प्रतिशत हो जाता है। मूल मिश्रण की मात्रा क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"25 liters","hi":"25 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"30 liters","hi":"30 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"35 liters","hi":"35 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"40 liters","hi":"40 लीटर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the original mixture be \\(x\\) litres, with acid \\(0.2x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{0.2x}{x + 10} = 0.15\\)<br>\\(0.2x = 0.15x + 1.5 \\Rightarrow 0.05x = 1.5\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{30}\\) litres<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 30 liters.</b>","hi":"मूल मिश्रण \\(x\\) लीटर मानिए, अम्ल \\(0.2x\\)<br>\\(\\frac{0.2x}{x + 10} = 0.15\\)<br>\\(0.2x = 0.15x + 1.5 \\Rightarrow 0.05x = 1.5\\)<br>\\(x = \\boxed{30}\\) लीटर<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 30 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000071242","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks an article's price 30% above its cost price. He then offers a 10% discount on the marked price when selling it. What is his overall profit percentage? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार किसी वस्तु का मूल्य उसके लागत मूल्य से 30% अधिक अंकित करता है। फिर वह बेचते समय अंकित मूल्य पर 10% छूट देता है। उसका कुल लाभ प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19%"},"2":{"en":"20%"},"3":{"en":"17%"},"4":{"en":"22%"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let CP = 100, then MP = 130<br>SP = \\(130 \\times 0.90 = 117\\)<br>Profit = \\(117 - 100 = 17\\)<br>Profit % = \\(\\boxed{17\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 17%.</b>","hi":"लागत मूल्य = 100, अतः अंकित मूल्य = 130<br>विक्रय मूल्य = \\(130 \\times 0.90 = 117\\)<br>लाभ = \\(117 - 100 = 17\\)<br>लाभ % = \\(\\boxed{17\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 17% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000071243","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right circular cylinder has a height of 8 m. If four times the combined area of its two circular bases is equal to three times its curved surface area, find the radius of the base (in m). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समकोणीय वृत्तीय बेलन की ऊँचाई 8 m है। यदि इसके दोनों वृत्तीय आधारों के संयुक्त क्षेत्रफल का चार गुना इसके वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल के तीन गुना के बराबर है, तो आधार की त्रिज्या (m में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 m"},"2":{"en":"6 m"},"3":{"en":"7 m"},"4":{"en":"8 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Area of both bases = \\(2\\pi r^2\\); curved surface area = \\(2\\pi rh\\)<br>\\(4(2\\pi r^2) = 3(2\\pi rh) \\Rightarrow 8\\pi r^2 = 6\\pi r h\\)<br>\\(8r = 6h = 6 \\times 8 = 48\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{6}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6 m.</b>","hi":"दोनों आधारों का क्षेत्रफल = \\(2\\pi r^2\\); वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(2\\pi rh\\)<br>\\(4(2\\pi r^2) = 3(2\\pi rh) \\Rightarrow 8\\pi r^2 = 6\\pi r h\\)<br>\\(8r = 6h = 6 \\times 8 = 48\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{6}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000071244","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"The difference between the squares of two consecutive odd numbers is 128. What is the square root of their sum? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो क्रमागत विषम संख्याओं के वर्गों का अंतर 128 है। उनके योग का वर्गमूल क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"10"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the smaller odd number be \\(n\\) and the next consecutive odd number be \\(n + 2\\).<br>\\((n + 2)^2 - n^2 = 4n + 4 = 128 \\Rightarrow n = 31\\)<br>So the numbers are 31 and 33; their sum is \\(31 + 33 = 64\\).<br>Square root of the sum = \\(\\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 8.</b>","hi":"छोटी विषम संख्या \\(n\\) और अगली क्रमागत विषम संख्या \\(n + 2\\) मानिए।<br>\\((n + 2)^2 - n^2 = 4n + 4 = 128 \\Rightarrow n = 31\\)<br>अतः संख्याएँ 31 और 33 हैं; उनका योग \\(31 + 33 = 64\\) है।<br>योग का वर्गमूल = \\(\\sqrt{64} = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000071245","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"A car worth ₹5,00,000 depreciates at 8% in the first year, 12% in the second year, and 10% in the third year. Find its value after 3 years. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹5,00,000 मूल्य की एक कार का मूल्य पहले वर्ष 8%, दूसरे वर्ष 12% और तीसरे वर्ष 10% घटता है। 3 वर्षों बाद उसका मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹4,45,391"},"2":{"en":"₹1,34,381"},"3":{"en":"₹3,64,320"},"4":{"en":"₹2,37,634"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Value = \\(500000 \\times 0.92 \\times 0.88 \\times 0.90\\)<br>\\(= 500000 \\times 0.72864\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3{,}64{,}320}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹3,64,320.</b>","hi":"मूल्य = \\(500000 \\times 0.92 \\times 0.88 \\times 0.90\\)<br>\\(= 500000 \\times 0.72864\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3{,}64{,}320}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹3,64,320 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000071246","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A cooperative bank lends ₹5,00,000 to a trader at simple interest. After 8 years, he repays a total amount of ₹7,00,000 to settle the loan. Another trader borrows ₹7,50,000 at the same rate but for 12 years. Calculate the difference in interest paid by the second trader compared to the first. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक सहकारी बैंक एक व्यापारी को साधारण ब्याज पर ₹5,00,000 उधार देता है। 8 वर्षों बाद वह ऋण चुकाने के लिए कुल ₹7,00,000 लौटाता है। दूसरा व्यापारी उसी दर पर ₹7,50,000, परंतु 12 वर्षों के लिए उधार लेता है। दूसरे व्यापारी द्वारा पहले की तुलना में दिए गए ब्याज का अंतर ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,80,000"},"2":{"en":"₹2,25,000"},"3":{"en":"₹2,50,000"},"4":{"en":"₹1,50,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Interest of the first trader = \\(7{,}00{,}000 - 5{,}00{,}000 = 2{,}00{,}000\\)<br>\\(2{,}00{,}000 = \\frac{5{,}00{,}000 \\times r \\times 8}{100} \\Rightarrow r = 5\\%\\)<br>Interest of the second trader = \\(\\frac{7{,}50{,}000 \\times 5 \\times 12}{100} = 4{,}50{,}000\\)<br>Difference = \\(4{,}50{,}000 - 2{,}00{,}000 = \\boxed{2{,}50{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹2,50,000.</b>","hi":"पहले व्यापारी का ब्याज = \\(7{,}00{,}000 - 5{,}00{,}000 = 2{,}00{,}000\\)<br>\\(2{,}00{,}000 = \\frac{5{,}00{,}000 \\times r \\times 8}{100} \\Rightarrow r = 5\\%\\)<br>दूसरे व्यापारी का ब्याज = \\(\\frac{7{,}50{,}000 \\times 5 \\times 12}{100} = 4{,}50{,}000\\)<br>अंतर = \\(4{,}50{,}000 - 2{,}00{,}000 = \\boxed{2{,}50{,}000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹2,50,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000071247","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"Three competing startups - A, B and C - generate annual revenues in the ratio of 7:9:12. Their annual operating expenditures are in the ratio 8:9:15, respectively. If A saves 1/4th of its annual revenue as profit, what is the ratio of the annual profits of A, B and C, respectively? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"तीन प्रतिस्पर्धी स्टार्टअप - A, B और C - की वार्षिक आय क्रमशः 7:9:12 के अनुपात में है। उनके वार्षिक परिचालन व्यय क्रमशः 8:9:15 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि A अपनी वार्षिक आय का 1/4 भाग लाभ के रूप में बचाता है, तो A, B और C के वार्षिक लाभों का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"65:99:70"},"2":{"en":"56:90:67"},"3":{"en":"60:68:65"},"4":{"en":"56:99:69"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let revenues be \\(7x, 9x, 12x\\) and expenditures \\(8y, 9y, 15y\\).<br>A's profit = \\(\\frac{1}{4} \\times 7x = 1.75x\\), so \\(7x - 8y = 1.75x \\Rightarrow 8y = 5.25x \\Rightarrow y = 0.65625x\\)<br>Profits: A = \\(1.75x\\), B = \\(9x - 5.90625x = 3.09375x\\), C = \\(12x - 9.84375x = 2.15625x\\)<br>Ratio = \\(1.75 : 3.09375 : 2.15625 = 56 : 99 : 69\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{56:99:69}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 56:99:69.</b>","hi":"आय \\(7x, 9x, 12x\\) और व्यय \\(8y, 9y, 15y\\) मानिए।<br>A का लाभ = \\(\\frac{1}{4} \\times 7x = 1.75x\\), अतः \\(7x - 8y = 1.75x \\Rightarrow 8y = 5.25x \\Rightarrow y = 0.65625x\\)<br>लाभ: A = \\(1.75x\\), B = \\(9x - 5.90625x = 3.09375x\\), C = \\(12x - 9.84375x = 2.15625x\\)<br>अनुपात = \\(1.75 : 3.09375 : 2.15625 = 56 : 99 : 69\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{56:99:69}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 56:99:69 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000071248","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A team of 12 workers can complete a project in 15 days by working 8 hrs a day. After working for 5 days, 4 workers fall sick and leave the project. The management requests the remaining workers to complete the project in the originally scheduled 15 days due to urgency. How many hours a day must the remaining workers work to complete the work within the specified time? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"12 श्रमिकों की एक टीम प्रतिदिन 8 घंटे कार्य करके एक परियोजना 15 दिनों में पूरी कर सकती है। 5 दिन कार्य करने के बाद 4 श्रमिक बीमार पड़कर परियोजना छोड़ देते हैं। प्रबंधन तात्कालिकता के कारण शेष श्रमिकों से मूल निर्धारित 15 दिनों में ही परियोजना पूरी करने का अनुरोध करता है। निर्धारित समय में कार्य पूरा करने के लिए शेष श्रमिकों को प्रतिदिन कितने घंटे कार्य करना होगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 hrs","hi":"12 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"11 hrs","hi":"11 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"10 hrs","hi":"10 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"9 hrs","hi":"9 घंटे"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Total work = \\(12 \\times 8 \\times 15 = 1440\\) man-hours<br>Work done in 5 days = \\(12 \\times 8 \\times 5 = 480\\); remaining = 960 man-hours<br>Remaining workers = 8, days left = 10, so hours per day = \\(\\frac{960}{8 \\times 10}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12}\\) hrs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 12 hrs.</b>","hi":"कुल कार्य = \\(12 \\times 8 \\times 15 = 1440\\) श्रमिक-घंटे<br>5 दिनों में किया गया कार्य = \\(12 \\times 8 \\times 5 = 480\\); शेष = 960 श्रमिक-घंटे<br>शेष श्रमिक = 8, शेष दिन = 10, अतः प्रतिदिन घंटे = \\(\\frac{960}{8 \\times 10}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 12 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000071249","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Simplify: \\(\\sin\\theta \\cdot \\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta) - \\cos\\theta \\cdot \\csc(90^\\circ-\\theta) + \\tan\\theta \\cdot \\cot(90^\\circ-\\theta)\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरल कीजिए: \\(\\sin\\theta \\cdot \\sec(90^\\circ-\\theta) - \\cos\\theta \\cdot \\csc(90^\\circ-\\theta) + \\tan\\theta \\cdot \\cot(90^\\circ-\\theta)\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sin^2\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\tan^2\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\csc\\theta\\), \\(\\csc(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sec\\theta\\), \\(\\cot(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\tan\\theta\\)<br>Expression = \\(\\sin\\theta\\csc\\theta - \\cos\\theta\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\boxed{\\tan^2\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\tan^2\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\csc\\theta\\), \\(\\csc(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\sec\\theta\\), \\(\\cot(90^\\circ - \\theta) = \\tan\\theta\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\(\\sin\\theta\\csc\\theta - \\cos\\theta\\sec\\theta + \\tan\\theta\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(= 1 - 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = \\boxed{\\tan^2\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\tan^2\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000071250","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"A survey was conducted among 200 students to find out the distance they travel from their homes to school every day.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_EN.jpg?edu=639294381003718127\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>Read the graph and answer the following question.<br>How many students travel 10 km or more to reach school?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_EN.jpg?edu=639294381003718127\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"200 विद्यार्थियों के बीच सर्वेक्षण किया गया कि वे प्रतिदिन अपने घर से स्कूल तक कितनी दूरी तय करते हैं।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_HI.jpg?edu=639294381120315945\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>ग्राफ पढ़िए और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>कितने विद्यार्थी स्कूल पहुँचने के लिए 10 km या उससे अधिक यात्रा करते हैं?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_HI.jpg?edu=639294381120315945\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45"},"2":{"en":"70"},"3":{"en":"50"},"4":{"en":"90"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the graph the percentages are: 0–5 km → 20%, 5–10 km → 35%, 10–15 km → 25%, 15–20 km → 12.5%, 20–25 km → 7.5%<br>Students travelling 10 km or more = \\(25\\% + 12.5\\% + 7.5\\% = 45\\%\\)<br>\\(= 45\\%\\) of 200 = \\(\\boxed{90}\\) students<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 90.</b>","hi":"ग्राफ से प्रतिशत हैं: 0–5 km → 20%, 5–10 km → 35%, 10–15 km → 25%, 15–20 km → 12.5%, 20–25 km → 7.5%<br>10 km या अधिक यात्रा करने वाले विद्यार्थी = \\(25\\% + 12.5\\% + 7.5\\% = 45\\%\\)<br>\\(= 200\\) का \\(45\\%\\) = \\(\\boxed{90}\\) विद्यार्थी<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 90 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_EN.jpg?edu=639294381003718127","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019ecfc0-286e-72f3-83f6-b8304439cfb8_HI.jpg?edu=639294381120315945"]}},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000071251","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Points A and B lie on the same straight horizontal line, on the same side of a vertical hill. The angle of elevation of the top of the hill from A is 30°, and from B is 45°. The distance between A and B is 20 m, with B closer to the hill. Find the height of the hill. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"बिंदु A और B एक ही सीधी क्षैतिज रेखा पर, एक ऊर्ध्वाधर पहाड़ी के एक ही ओर स्थित हैं। पहाड़ी के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण A से 30° और B से 45° है। A और B के बीच की दूरी 20 m है, जिसमें B पहाड़ी के अधिक निकट है। पहाड़ी की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(20(\\sqrt{3} - 1)\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(20(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(10(1 + \\sqrt{3})\\) m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From B: \\(h = d\\tan 45^\\circ = d\\)<br>From A: \\(h = (d + 20)\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{d + 20}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>So \\(d\\sqrt{3} = d + 20 \\Rightarrow d(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 20 \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3} - 1}\\)<br>\\(h = d = \\frac{20(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{3 - 1} = \\boxed{10(1 + \\sqrt{3})}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(10(1 + \\sqrt{3})\\) m.</b>","hi":"B से: \\(h = d\\tan 45^\\circ = d\\)<br>A से: \\(h = (d + 20)\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{d + 20}{\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>अतः \\(d\\sqrt{3} = d + 20 \\Rightarrow d(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 20 \\Rightarrow d = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{3} - 1}\\)<br>\\(h = d = \\frac{20(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{3 - 1} = \\boxed{10(1 + \\sqrt{3})}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(10(1 + \\sqrt{3})\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000071252","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following radical expression completely: \\(\\sqrt[3]{54} + \\sqrt[3]{128} - \\sqrt[3]{16}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित करणी व्यंजक को पूर्णतः सरल कीजिए: \\(\\sqrt[3]{54} + \\sqrt[3]{128} - \\sqrt[3]{16}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(9\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(7\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{54} = \\sqrt[3]{27 \\times 2} = 3\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{128} = \\sqrt[3]{64 \\times 2} = 4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{16} = \\sqrt[3]{8 \\times 2} = 2\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>Sum = \\((3 + 4 - 2)\\sqrt[3]{2} = \\boxed{5\\sqrt[3]{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(5\\sqrt[3]{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt[3]{54} = \\sqrt[3]{27 \\times 2} = 3\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{128} = \\sqrt[3]{64 \\times 2} = 4\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt[3]{16} = \\sqrt[3]{8 \\times 2} = 2\\sqrt[3]{2}\\)<br>योग = \\((3 + 4 - 2)\\sqrt[3]{2} = \\boxed{5\\sqrt[3]{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(5\\sqrt[3]{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000071253","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(X = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{5}}\\), then find the value of \\(X + \\frac{1}{X}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(X = \\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{5}}\\) है, तो \\(X + \\frac{1}{X}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rationalising: \\(X = \\frac{(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^2}{7 - 5} = \\frac{12 + 2\\sqrt{35}}{2} = 6 + \\sqrt{35}\\)<br>Then \\(\\frac{1}{X} = 6 - \\sqrt{35}\\)<br>\\(X + \\frac{1}{X} = 12\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12.</b>","hi":"परिमेयकरण: \\(X = \\frac{(\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{5})^2}{7 - 5} = \\frac{12 + 2\\sqrt{35}}{2} = 6 + \\sqrt{35}\\)<br>तब \\(\\frac{1}{X} = 6 - \\sqrt{35}\\)<br>\\(X + \\frac{1}{X} = 12\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{12}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000071254","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The double bar graph shows the Video Lecture Completion Rate (%) and the Average Assignment Quiz Score (%) across four different professional certification paths.<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_EN.jpg?edu=639294381005037362\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>A platform calculates an Engagement Efficiency Score (EES) for each path using the formula: EES = (Video Lecture Completion Rate × Average Assignment Quiz Score) / 100. What is the absolute difference in the EES between the certification path with the highest score and the certification path with the lowest score?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_EN.jpg?edu=639294381005037362\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दोहरा स्तंभ ग्राफ चार भिन्न व्यावसायिक प्रमाणन पथों में वीडियो लेक्चर पूर्णता दर (%) और औसत असाइनमेंट क्विज़ स्कोर (%) दर्शाता है।<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_HI.jpg?edu=639294381121031265\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"><br>एक प्लेटफ़ॉर्म सूत्र EES = (वीडियो लेक्चर पूर्णता दर × औसत असाइनमेंट क्विज़ स्कोर) / 100 से प्रत्येक पथ के लिए एंगेजमेंट एफिशिएंसी स्कोर (EES) निकालता है। सर्वाधिक स्कोर वाले और न्यूनतम स्कोर वाले प्रमाणन पथ के EES में निरपेक्ष अंतर क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_HI.jpg?edu=639294381121031265\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.30"},"2":{"en":"3.00"},"3":{"en":"6.40"},"4":{"en":"8.70"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"From the graph: Data Science → 75%, 82%; Cybersecurity → 60%, 88%; Cloud Computing → 80%, 74%; AI Engineering → 65%, 90%<br>EES: Data Science = \\(\\frac{75 \\times 82}{100} = 61.5\\); Cybersecurity = \\(\\frac{60 \\times 88}{100} = 52.8\\); Cloud = \\(\\frac{80 \\times 74}{100} = 59.2\\); AI = \\(\\frac{65 \\times 90}{100} = 58.5\\)<br>Difference = \\(61.5 - 52.8 = \\boxed{8.70}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.70.</b>","hi":"ग्राफ से: Data Science → 75%, 82%; Cybersecurity → 60%, 88%; Cloud Computing → 80%, 74%; AI Engineering → 65%, 90%<br>EES: Data Science = \\(\\frac{75 \\times 82}{100} = 61.5\\); Cybersecurity = \\(\\frac{60 \\times 88}{100} = 52.8\\); Cloud = \\(\\frac{80 \\times 74}{100} = 59.2\\); AI = \\(\\frac{65 \\times 90}{100} = 58.5\\)<br>अंतर = \\(61.5 - 52.8 = \\boxed{8.70}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8.70 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/EN/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_EN.jpg?edu=639294381005037362","https://sscexams.cbexams.com/CGLE2026jsdgheQchallengemshetsOct24/qimg/3/HI/019f89a2-9a35-7fab-b427-3831295dda4d_HI.jpg?edu=639294381121031265"]}},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000071255","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Which of the following is identically equal to (m + n)³ + (m − n)³? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा (m + n)³ + (m − n)³ के तत्समक रूप से बराबर है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2m(m^2 + 3n^2)\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2m(3m^2 + n^2)\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(2n(3m^2 + n^2)\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2(m^3 + n^3)\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((a + b)^3 + (a - b)^3 = 2a^3 + 6ab^2\\) with \\(a = m\\), \\(b = n\\)<br>\\(= 2m^3 + 6mn^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2m(m^2 + 3n^2)}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(2m(m^2 + 3n^2)\\).</b>","hi":"\\((a + b)^3 + (a - b)^3 = 2a^3 + 6ab^2\\), जहाँ \\(a = m\\), \\(b = n\\)<br>\\(= 2m^3 + 6mn^2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2m(m^2 + 3n^2)}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(2m(m^2 + 3n^2)\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000071256","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.<br>The professor gave a <b>lucid</b> explanation of the concept. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Confusing"},"2":{"en":"Clear"},"3":{"en":"Dark"},"4":{"en":"Complicated"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Lucid (स्पष्ट) = clear and easy to understand.</b><br><b>Confusing (भ्रमित)</b> = unclear<br><b>Clear (स्पष्ट)</b> = easy to understand ✔<br><b>Dark (अंधेरा)</b> = obscure; <b>complicated (जटिल)</b> = complex; synonyms: coherent, intelligible.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Clear.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000071257","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.<br>The researcher was <b>meticulous</b> in recording data. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Careless"},"2":{"en":"Hasty"},"3":{"en":"Thorough"},"4":{"en":"Casual"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Meticulous (सूक्ष्मता से काम करने वाला) = extremely careful and precise.</b><br><b>Careless (लापरवाह)</b> = negligent<br><b>Hasty (जल्दबाज)</b> = rushed<br><b>Thorough (पूर्ण)</b> = complete and careful ✔<br><b>Casual (आकस्मिक)</b> = informal or unconcerned.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Thorough.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000071258","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The team's <b>morose</b> attitude after the defeat was visible to everyone. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gloomy"},"2":{"en":"Sullen"},"3":{"en":"Cheerful"},"4":{"en":"Glum"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Morose (उदास) = gloomy and sullen.</b><br><b>Gloomy (उदास)</b> = depressed<br><b>Sullen (खिन्न)</b> = resentfully silent<br><b>Cheerful (प्रसन्न)</b> = happy ✔<br><b>Glum (उदास)</b> = dejected.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Cheerful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000071259","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The young pop star was surrounded by the <b>adulation</b> of her millions of fans. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Criticism"},"2":{"en":"Praise"},"3":{"en":"Worship"},"4":{"en":"Flattery"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Adulation (अत्यधिक प्रशंसा) = excessive admiration.</b><br><b>Criticism (आलोचना)</b> = disapproval ✔<br><b>Praise (प्रशंसा)</b> = approval<br><b>Worship (पूजा)</b> = reverence; <b>flattery (चापलूसी)</b> = excessive praise.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Criticism.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000071260","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>The <b>buraeu</b> was made of solid oak. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Buro"},"2":{"en":"Buraeu"},"3":{"en":"Burau"},"4":{"en":"Bureau"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Bureau (कार्यालय/अलमारी) = an office or a writing desk.</b><br>The correct spelling is “bureau.”<br><b>Buro</b> omits letters; <b>buraeu</b> reverses vowels.<br><b>Burau</b> omits “e.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Bureau.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000071261","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>The new business was launched on an <b>auspiciouss</b> day. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Auspiciouss"},"2":{"en":"Auspicious"},"3":{"en":"Auspiceous"},"4":{"en":"Auspisious"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Auspicious (शुभ) = favourable or promising success.</b><br>The correct spelling ends in a single “s.”<br><b>Auspiciouss</b> doubles the final “s.”<br><b>Auspiceous</b> and <b>auspisious</b> use incorrect vowel patterns.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Auspicious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000071262","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Pick out the homonym from the given options that can suitably complete both Sentence (P) and Sentence (Q) given below.<br>(P) Audio engineers deliberately introduced harmonic ___ into the guitar's vacuum-tube amplifier circuit to cultivate the gritty, saturated sonic texture essential for rock music production.<br>(Q) Political scientists warn that the systematic, intentional ___ of historical facts by partisan media outlets severely polarises the electorate and undermines democratic discourse. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manipulation"},"2":{"en":"Modulation"},"3":{"en":"distortion"},"4":{"en":"corruption"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Distortion = alteration of sound or of factual truth.</b><br>Harmonic distortion creates the gritty texture of an amplified guitar.<br>Distortion of facts misrepresents history and damages democratic discourse.<br>The other options do not fit both scientific and political contexts.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): distortion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000071263","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Which of the following options most accurately expresses the meaning of the idiom “to fly a kite”? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To indulge in trivial, non-productive recreational distractions during critical corporate working hours to evade administrative duties."},"2":{"en":"To harness atmospheric wind patterns through innovative, non-traditional renewable energy technologies to power local manufacturing grids."},"3":{"en":"To experience an overwhelming sensation of creative euphoria or psychological detachment during a complex brainstorming session."},"4":{"en":"To intentionally introduce a controversial policy or speculative idea to the public to gauge collective reactions and opinions."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Fly a kite (जनप्रतिक्रिया जाँचना) = float an idea to test public reaction.</b><br>Example: “The minister flew a kite about tax reform.”<br>The idiom is figurative and does not concern recreation or wind energy.<br>Its purpose is assessing responses to a tentative proposal.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): To intentionally introduce a controversial policy or speculative idea to the public to gauge collective reactions and opinions..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000071264","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"The sentence given below is divided into four segments labelled P, Q, R, and S. Read the sentence carefully to determine which segment contains a lexical error. Select the letter corresponding to that specific segment as your answer. (Note: The sentence contains exactly one error. Ignore errors of punctuation, if any.)<br>(P) Despite a lucid awareness of catastrophic epidemiological outcomes, / (Q) active smokers frequently suffer from severe confident dissonance, / (R) systematically deploying deeply flawed psychological defence mechanisms to manipulate their internal narrative, / (S) minimise perceived vulnerability, and ultimately preserve the habituated patterns of their addictive behaviour. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P"},"2":{"en":"Q"},"3":{"en":"R"},"4":{"en":"S"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The established term is “cognitive dissonance.”</b><br>Segment Q incorrectly uses “confident dissonance.”<br>It means psychological discomfort from holding conflicting beliefs or actions.<br>The other segments are lexically sound.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Q.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000071265","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"The sentence given below is divided into four segments labelled P, Q, R, and S. Read the sentence carefully to determine which segment contains a lexical error. Select the letter corresponding to that specific segment as your answer. (Note: The sentence contains exactly one error. Ignore errors of punctuation, if any.)<br>(P) The prime minister faced intense scrutiny from legislative oversight committees / (Q) after appointing his brother-in-law to head the central bank, a nepotistic appointment / (R) widely criticised as a blatant conflict of impress by anti-corruption watchdogs / (S) demanding an immediate, independent inquiry into executive overreach. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"P"},"2":{"en":"Q"},"3":{"en":"R"},"4":{"en":"S"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Conflict of interest” is the standard expression.</b><br>Segment R incorrectly uses “conflict of impress.”<br>The appointment allegedly created competing personal and public interests.<br>The other segments are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): R.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000071266","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks with the most appropriate combination of articles and verb form.<br>It is imperative that ___ anonymity of the whistle-blower ___ maintained, as even ___ slightest leak could compromise the entire federal investigation. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"no article, is, a"},"2":{"en":"an, be, a"},"3":{"en":"the, is, the"},"4":{"en":"the, be, the"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Mandative “imperative” takes the base subjunctive “be.”</b><br>Specific anonymity takes “the,” and “the slightest” is a fixed emphatic phrase.<br>“The anonymity … be maintained” is correct.<br>The other combinations use the wrong article or indicative verb.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): the, be, the.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000071267","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the following sentence carefully and focus on the underlined portion. Choose the option (A, B, or C) that best substitutes the underlined segment to improve the sentence grammatically or contextually. If the sentence is correct as written, select Option D (No Improvement Required).<br>The longitudinal neuroimaging study was designed <b>to map slowly the degradation of neural pathways over six months</b>, deliberately altering the control group's environment. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"to map slowly the degradation of neural pathways over six months"},"2":{"en":"to map the degradation slowly of neural pathways over six months"},"3":{"en":"to slowly map over six months the degradation of neural pathways"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>The original adverb placement is acceptable.</b><br>“Slowly” modifies the mapping of neural degradation over six months.<br>The alternatives either split the noun phrase awkwardly or displace the duration.<br>No improvement is required.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): No improvement required.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000071268","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the following sentence carefully, focusing on the underlined portion. Select the option (A/B/C) that can suitably substitute the underlined segment to improve the given sentence. If the sentence is correct as written, then select Option D (No improvement required).<br>The enigmatic polymath, as well as her newly appointed research fellows, <b>were heavily criticised by the oversight committee for failing to document their experimental methodology</b> before the launch of the clinical trials. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"was heavily criticised by the oversight committee for failing to document his"},"2":{"en":"were heavily criticised by the oversight committee for failing to document its"},"3":{"en":"was heavily criticised by the oversight committee for failing to document her"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “As well as” does not change agreement with the singular head subject.</b><br>“Polymath” is singular and takes “was.”<br>The earlier pronoun “her” identifies the researcher as female, so “her methodology” is appropriate.<br>Only C corrects both verb and pronoun.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): was heavily criticised by the oversight committee for failing to document her.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000071269","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the following sentence from direct to indirect speech. Select the option that correctly applies tense shift, pronoun change, and maintains grammatical accuracy.<br>Avani said to Shanaya, “Instantly I remembered that during my youth I followed my mother around our home, the two of us singing about how a legendary warrior fought gloriously and returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community.” [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Avani told Shanaya that instantly she had remembered that during her young she had followed her mother around their home, the two of them singing about how a legendary warrior had fought gloriously and had returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community."},"2":{"en":"Avani told Shanaya that instantly she had remembered that during her youth she had followed her mother around their home, the two of them singing about how a legendary warrior had fought gloriously and had returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community."},"3":{"en":"Avani told Shanaya that instantly she had remembered that during her young she had followed her mother around their home, the two of them singing about how a legendary warrior had fought glorious and had returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community."},"4":{"en":"Avani told Shanaya that instantly she had remembered that during her youth she had been following her mother around their home, the two of them singing about how a legendary warrior had fought glorious and had returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past reporting shifts simple past to past perfect and adjusts pronouns.</b><br>“I” becomes “she,” “my mother” becomes “her mother,” and “our” becomes “their.”<br>“Youth” is the correct noun, and the adverb “gloriously” must be retained.<br>Only B preserves all these features.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Avani told Shanaya that instantly she had remembered that during her youth she had followed her mother around their home, the two of them singing about how a legendary warrior had fought gloriously and had returned safely from a conflict to settle in his community..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000071270","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Select the option that correctly converts the following indirect statement into direct speech.<br>Shruti told Manas that outside the station she had been waiting, and then her friend had merely sung, which was so typical, telling her to follow her, but not as though she were doing so, until they came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Shruti said to Manas, “Outside the station I was waiting, and then my friend merely sang, which is so typical, 'Follow me, but not as though you are doing so,' until we came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab.”"},"2":{"en":"Shruti said to Manas, “Outside the station I had waited, and then my friend merely sang, which is so typical, 'Follow me, but not as though you are doing so,' until we came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab.”"},"3":{"en":"Shruti said to Manas, “Outside the station I was waiting, and then my friend merely sung, which is so typical, 'Follow me, but not as though you are doing so,' until we came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab.”"},"4":{"en":"Shruti said to Manas, “Outside the station I was waiting, and then my friend merely sang, which is so typical, ‘Followed me, but not as though you are doing so,' until we came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab.”"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Reverse tense shifts and restore the quoted imperative.</b><br>“Had been waiting” becomes “was waiting,” and “was” becomes “is.”<br>“Telling her to follow her” becomes “Follow me.”<br>Only A restores all the direct-speech details.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Shruti said to Manas, “Outside the station I was waiting, and then my friend merely sang, which is so typical, 'Follow me, but not as though you are doing so,' until we came to a tiny toll-house by the river, against which leant a faded cab.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000071271","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.<br>People reported that a massive fire broke out near the railway station. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was reported by people that a massive fire broke out nearby the railway station."},"2":{"en":"It was reported that a massive fire had broken out near the railway station."},"3":{"en":"A massive fire was reportedly to break out near the railway station."},"4":{"en":"It is reported that a massive fire broke out near the railway station."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “People reported” becomes “it was reported.”</b><br>The content clause can backshift “broke out” to “had broken out.”<br>The location phrase “near the railway station” remains unchanged.<br>B preserves the reporting past and the event accurately.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): It was reported that a massive fire had broken out near the railway station..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000071272","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"The following sentence has been divided into four parts (P, Q, R, and S). The last part (S5) is fixed. Rearrange the remaining parts to form a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence, and choose the correct sequence.<br>S1: The gods of the Greeks were not all-wise, all-powerful, and all-good, as we believe our God to be<br>P: are sometimes represented as depending upon mortals for information, and all these religious views tended to make the human form far more noble<br>Q: or omnipresent and was himself subject to the decrees of Fate, as when he could not save his loved Sarpedon from death, meaning that not knowing all things, even the gods<br>R: because if you read their mythology, you will find that with the power of the god, much imperfection and weakness were mingled, since<br>S: they did not believe that Zeus had been the greatest god from the beginning, but that there was a time when he had no power, nor was he omniscient<br>S5: to the Greek than it can be to the Christian, with his different views of the relations of God and man. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QRSP"},"2":{"en":"RSQP"},"3":{"en":"PQRS"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RSQP</b><br>R introduces mythology’s mixture of divine power and weakness.<br>S and Q explain Zeus’s limits in knowledge, presence and submission to Fate.<br>P concludes with dependence on mortals and the nobility of the human form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RSQP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000071273","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Five sentence fragments—P, Q, R, S, and T—are given in a jumbled order. Four of these fragments can be arranged to form a single grammatically and logically coherent sentence, while one fragment does not fit the meaning or structure. Identify the correct sequence of the four relevant fragments, ignoring the irrelevant one, and select the correct option from the given choices.<br>P: in the summer of 1991, Pinatubo, a volcano in the Philippines, started erupting on June 12 and culminated in a tremendous<br>Q: those scientists saved countless lives, but their forecast of the eruption was more of an educated guess than<br>R: while killing more than 800 people, when their roofs, weighed down by rain-saturated ash, collapsed<br>S: explosion three days later, and by the time pyroclastic flows, which are incandescent avalanches of molten rock and gas<br>T: tumbled down its sterilised slopes, Pinatubo’s peak had been obliterated and replaced by a 2.5-kilometre-wide chasm [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PSTR"},"2":{"en":"TQRS"},"3":{"en":"QRPS"},"4":{"en":"PRQS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: P-S-T-R</b><br>P and S describe the eruption and pyroclastic flows.<br>T continues the flows down the slopes and describes the resulting chasm.<br>R adds the deaths caused by collapsing roofs; Q is incomplete and irrelevant.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PSTR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000071274","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to complete the sentence meaningfully and grammatically.<br>The director ___ the entire script multiple times before the producers finally ___ it last week. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"has rewritten, approve"},"2":{"en":"had rewritten, approved"},"3":{"en":"rewrites, approve"},"4":{"en":"was rewriting, approved"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect marks repeated rewriting before the later approval.</b><br>The producers approved the script last week in simple past.<br>The director had rewritten it multiple times before that point.<br>Only B establishes the sequence correctly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): had rewritten, approved.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000071275","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"A sentence in the Passive Voice is given below. From the four alternatives, choose the one that best expresses the same sentence in the Active Voice.<br>The crew members of the Astronef are expected by Lord Redgrave to test the anti-gravitational engines thoroughly before their voyage to Venus. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Redgrave expected the anti-gravitational engines to be thoroughly tested by the crew members of the Astronef before their voyage to Venus."},"2":{"en":"Lord Redgrave expected the crew members of the Astronef to thoroughly test the anti-gravitational engines before their voyage to Venus."},"3":{"en":"Lord Redgrave expects the crew members of the Astronef to thoroughly test the anti-gravitational engines before their voyage to Venus."},"4":{"en":"Lord Redgrave is expecting the anti-gravitational engines to be thoroughly tested by the crew members of the Astronef before their voyage to Venus."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Are expected” becomes active simple present “expects.”</b><br>Lord Redgrave becomes the subject and the crew members the object of “expects.”<br>The infinitive becomes active: “to thoroughly test.”<br>Only C retains present tense and removes the passive construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Lord Redgrave expects the crew members of the Astronef to thoroughly test the anti-gravitational engines before their voyage to Venus..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000071276","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>Ocean exploration, once confined to myth and imagination, has evolved into a disciplined scientific pursuit that reshapes our understanding of Earth’s final frontier, particularly in the context of climate change and resource scarcity, where the oceans are increasingly viewed as both a frontier and a reservoir of critical knowledge.<br><br>Modern expeditions, driven by advanced submersibles and satellite-linked technologies, (A)___ reveal previously inaccessible marine ecosystems that challenge conventional biological theories, thereby expanding the boundaries of contemporary oceanography and interdisciplinary research.<br><br>In recent decades, oceanographers have achieved remarkable breakthroughs in mapping the seabed; (B)___, the vastness and pressure of the deep ocean continue to hinder comprehensive data collection and slow the pace of scientific validation.<br><br>Ongoing deep-sea missions often (C)___ previously held assumptions about marine biodiversity, compelling scientists to revise established classifications within modern marine taxonomy.<br><br>The discovery of hydrothermal vents has added a new dimension to marine science, highlighting the (D)___ nature of life forms thriving in extreme conditions and reshaping prevailing notions of biological adaptability in the abyssal zone.<br><br>These insights underscore the importance of sustained investment in oceanic research (E)___ global environmental sustainability and the long-term preservation of marine ecosystems.<br><br><br>In the context of the passage, choose the correct option to fill in blank (A). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"continually"},"2":{"en":"distinctively"},"3":{"en":"subsequently"},"4":{"en":"enthusiastically"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Continually (निरंतर) = repeatedly over time.</b><br>Modern expeditions continually reveal inaccessible ecosystems.<br>“Distinctively” concerns uniqueness, “subsequently” sequence.<br>“Enthusiastically” describes emotion rather than scientific progress.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): continually.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000071277","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>Ocean exploration, once confined to myth and imagination, has evolved into a disciplined scientific pursuit that reshapes our understanding of Earth’s final frontier, particularly in the context of climate change and resource scarcity, where the oceans are increasingly viewed as both a frontier and a reservoir of critical knowledge.<br><br>Modern expeditions, driven by advanced submersibles and satellite-linked technologies, (A)___ reveal previously inaccessible marine ecosystems that challenge conventional biological theories, thereby expanding the boundaries of contemporary oceanography and interdisciplinary research.<br><br>In recent decades, oceanographers have achieved remarkable breakthroughs in mapping the seabed; (B)___, the vastness and pressure of the deep ocean continue to hinder comprehensive data collection and slow the pace of scientific validation.<br><br>Ongoing deep-sea missions often (C)___ previously held assumptions about marine biodiversity, compelling scientists to revise established classifications within modern marine taxonomy.<br><br>The discovery of hydrothermal vents has added a new dimension to marine science, highlighting the (D)___ nature of life forms thriving in extreme conditions and reshaping prevailing notions of biological adaptability in the abyssal zone.<br><br>These insights underscore the importance of sustained investment in oceanic research (E)___ global environmental sustainability and the long-term preservation of marine ecosystems.<br><br><br>Choose the most appropriate connector for blank (B). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"moreover"},"2":{"en":"therefore"},"3":{"en":"similarly"},"4":{"en":"however"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>However (फिर भी) introduces a contrast.</b><br>Mapping breakthroughs contrast with continuing difficulties in deep-ocean data collection.<br>“Moreover” adds information, “therefore” gives a result.<br>“Similarly” introduces comparison.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): however.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000071278","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>Ocean exploration, once confined to myth and imagination, has evolved into a disciplined scientific pursuit that reshapes our understanding of Earth’s final frontier, particularly in the context of climate change and resource scarcity, where the oceans are increasingly viewed as both a frontier and a reservoir of critical knowledge.<br><br>Modern expeditions, driven by advanced submersibles and satellite-linked technologies, (A)___ reveal previously inaccessible marine ecosystems that challenge conventional biological theories, thereby expanding the boundaries of contemporary oceanography and interdisciplinary research.<br><br>In recent decades, oceanographers have achieved remarkable breakthroughs in mapping the seabed; (B)___, the vastness and pressure of the deep ocean continue to hinder comprehensive data collection and slow the pace of scientific validation.<br><br>Ongoing deep-sea missions often (C)___ previously held assumptions about marine biodiversity, compelling scientists to revise established classifications within modern marine taxonomy.<br><br>The discovery of hydrothermal vents has added a new dimension to marine science, highlighting the (D)___ nature of life forms thriving in extreme conditions and reshaping prevailing notions of biological adaptability in the abyssal zone.<br><br>These insights underscore the importance of sustained investment in oceanic research (E)___ global environmental sustainability and the long-term preservation of marine ecosystems.<br><br><br>Identify the correct phrasal verb/idiom for blank (C). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"call into question"},"2":{"en":"bring forward"},"3":{"en":"set up"},"4":{"en":"look after"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Call into question (संदेह करना) = challenge an assumption.</b><br>Deep-sea missions challenge existing ideas about biodiversity.<br><b>Bring forward</b> = propose; <b>set up</b> = establish<br><b>Look after</b> = care for<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): call into question.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000071279","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>Ocean exploration, once confined to myth and imagination, has evolved into a disciplined scientific pursuit that reshapes our understanding of Earth’s final frontier, particularly in the context of climate change and resource scarcity, where the oceans are increasingly viewed as both a frontier and a reservoir of critical knowledge.<br><br>Modern expeditions, driven by advanced submersibles and satellite-linked technologies, (A)___ reveal previously inaccessible marine ecosystems that challenge conventional biological theories, thereby expanding the boundaries of contemporary oceanography and interdisciplinary research.<br><br>In recent decades, oceanographers have achieved remarkable breakthroughs in mapping the seabed; (B)___, the vastness and pressure of the deep ocean continue to hinder comprehensive data collection and slow the pace of scientific validation.<br><br>Ongoing deep-sea missions often (C)___ previously held assumptions about marine biodiversity, compelling scientists to revise established classifications within modern marine taxonomy.<br><br>The discovery of hydrothermal vents has added a new dimension to marine science, highlighting the (D)___ nature of life forms thriving in extreme conditions and reshaping prevailing notions of biological adaptability in the abyssal zone.<br><br>These insights underscore the importance of sustained investment in oceanic research (E)___ global environmental sustainability and the long-term preservation of marine ecosystems.<br><br><br>Select the most suitable word for blank (D). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"superficial"},"2":{"en":"irrelevant"},"3":{"en":"resilient"},"4":{"en":"volatile"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Resilient (लचीला) = able to survive and recover under difficult conditions.</b><br>Life around hydrothermal vents demonstrates resilience in extreme environments.<br>Superficial and irrelevant are inappropriate.<br>Volatile means unstable rather than adaptable.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): resilient.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000071280","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the following passage by filling in the blanks with the most appropriate words from the options given below.<br><br>Ocean exploration, once confined to myth and imagination, has evolved into a disciplined scientific pursuit that reshapes our understanding of Earth’s final frontier, particularly in the context of climate change and resource scarcity, where the oceans are increasingly viewed as both a frontier and a reservoir of critical knowledge.<br><br>Modern expeditions, driven by advanced submersibles and satellite-linked technologies, (A)___ reveal previously inaccessible marine ecosystems that challenge conventional biological theories, thereby expanding the boundaries of contemporary oceanography and interdisciplinary research.<br><br>In recent decades, oceanographers have achieved remarkable breakthroughs in mapping the seabed; (B)___, the vastness and pressure of the deep ocean continue to hinder comprehensive data collection and slow the pace of scientific validation.<br><br>Ongoing deep-sea missions often (C)___ previously held assumptions about marine biodiversity, compelling scientists to revise established classifications within modern marine taxonomy.<br><br>The discovery of hydrothermal vents has added a new dimension to marine science, highlighting the (D)___ nature of life forms thriving in extreme conditions and reshaping prevailing notions of biological adaptability in the abyssal zone.<br><br>These insights underscore the importance of sustained investment in oceanic research (E)___ global environmental sustainability and the long-term preservation of marine ecosystems.<br><br><br>Choose the correct prepositional phrase for blank (E). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"in pursuit of"},"2":{"en":"inspite of"},"3":{"en":"in accordance with"},"4":{"en":"at the cost of"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>In pursuit of (प्राप्ति के लिए) = with the aim of achieving.</b><br>Oceanic research is sustained in pursuit of environmental sustainability.<br>“In spite of” would signal contrast, and “at the cost of” implies sacrifice.<br>“In accordance with” means conforming to a rule.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): in pursuit of.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};